WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:49.801
[ Watch on KissFlix.co ]

2
00:50.071 --> 00:51.962
This is the admin office.

3
00:51.962 --> 00:55.626
All squad leaders, please submit today's list of soldiers

4
00:55.626 --> 00:58.482
returning from leave to the admin office.

5
00:58.482 --> 01:00.705
Once again.

6
01:00.705 --> 01:02.459
Today's list of soldiers returning from leave.

7
01:02.459 --> 01:05.681
All squad leaders, please submit it to the admin office.

8
01:05.681 --> 01:07.330
That is all.

9
01:07.330 --> 01:08.886
Do you always sound like that?

10
01:08.886 --> 01:10.236
Hey, what did that announcement say?

11
01:10.236 --> 01:11.953
I think they said to come get toilet paper.

12
01:11.953 --> 01:13.563
- I'm not sure either. - And that's it?

13
01:13.563 --> 01:14.545
Hey, go check with the admin office.

14
01:14.545 --> 01:15.846
- Yes. - I'll find out.

15
01:15.846 --> 01:18.078
Damn it. What is he even saying?

16
01:18.928 --> 01:20.235
What's the command center's extension?

17
01:20.235 --> 01:21.399
301.

18
01:21.399 --> 01:22.568
What's with your pronunciation?

19
01:22.568 --> 01:24.726
I can't tell if you're saying 301 or 302.

20
01:24.726 --> 01:26.570
301.

21
01:26.570 --> 01:28.329
What's the division commander's extension?

22
01:28.329 --> 01:30.740
- 307. - It's 306. 306.

23
01:30.740 --> 01:32.295
- Hold out your palm... - Yoon Mo, what did you say?

24
01:32.295 --> 01:33.953
Yoon Mo, what did you say?

25
01:33.953 --> 01:36.516
Chungseong! May I ask what he said?

26
01:36.516 --> 01:38.071
Yoon Mo, what did you say?

27
01:38.071 --> 01:39.100
Chungseong! Love you!

28
01:39.100 --> 01:41.193
Today's list of soldiers returning from leave...

29
01:41.193 --> 01:42.586
He said all squad leaders should submit

30
01:42.586 --> 01:45.102
today's list of soldiers returning from leave to the admin office.

31
01:45.102 --> 01:47.087
Train your guy properly.

32
01:47.087 --> 01:48.152
Yes. Sorry. Chungseong!

33
01:48.152 --> 01:50.415
- Let's go. - Yes.

34
01:50.415 --> 01:52.627
I couldn't understand a word.

35
01:54.337 --> 01:56.153
So where should I hit you today?

36
01:56.153 --> 01:58.551
- Huh? - Where do you want it?

37
01:58.551 --> 02:01.136
- Just once on the palm... - Let's do the back of your hand.

38
02:01.136 --> 02:02.554
One, two.

39
02:02.554 --> 02:05.012
Yoon Mo's palm never got a break.

40
02:05.012 --> 02:08.031
Isn't that hilarious?

41
02:08.031 --> 02:09.704
I mean, because of Yoon Mo,

42
02:09.704 --> 02:11.059
we're always having to go back to the admin office.

43
02:11.059 --> 02:13.275
It's a whole ordeal.

44
02:14.431 --> 02:16.053
Are you listening?

45
02:17.116 --> 02:18.955
Every time Yoon Mo makes an announcement,

46
02:18.955 --> 02:21.652
I can't understand a word he says.

47
02:21.652 --> 02:23.498
Seriously, he sounds like this.

48
02:23.498 --> 02:25.306
"This is the admin office.

49
02:25.306 --> 02:27.664
One Private First Class from each barracks..."

50
02:30.192 --> 02:32.131
Why'd you hit me all of a sudden?

51
02:32.131 --> 02:33.977
Thought I heard a mosquito.

52
02:33.977 --> 02:36.108
A mosquito? What are you talking about?

53
02:36.108 --> 02:38.504
You did that on purpose, didn't you?

54
02:38.504 --> 02:40.405
The weather's great,

55
02:40.405 --> 02:42.746
and I love driving around with you.

56
02:42.746 --> 02:44.142
Thanks for the ride.

57
02:44.142 --> 02:46.922
It's so hot, I'm already annoyed.

58
02:46.922 --> 02:49.837
If Dad hadn't ordered me to...

59
02:50.488 --> 02:51.931
Oh, right.

60
02:51.931 --> 02:54.804
Remember Sergeant Choi Il Gu? From mobilization training?

61
02:54.804 --> 02:57.539
I told you he came back as a staff sergeant, right?

62
02:59.081 --> 03:01.896
Staff Sergeant Choi Il Gu!

63
03:01.896 --> 03:04.277
Chungseong! Love you!

64
03:04.277 --> 03:07.187
Chungseong! Love you!

65
03:10.852 --> 03:13.402
Unit, attention!

66
03:15.478 --> 03:16.501
Salute Sergeant Choi Il Gu...

67
03:16.501 --> 03:18.940
No, Staff Sergeant Choi Il Gu!

68
03:18.940 --> 03:22.308
- Chungseong! Love you! - Chungseong! Love you!

69
03:22.308 --> 03:25.533
Chungseong! Love you!

70
03:25.533 --> 03:27.139
Good to see you again!

71
03:28.321 --> 03:30.794
We're really glad to see you too, Staff Sergeant.

72
03:33.016 --> 03:34.020
Choi Il Gu!

73
03:34.020 --> 03:37.017
Hey, let go, let go already.

74
03:37.017 --> 03:39.044
Chungseong! Love you!

75
03:39.044 --> 03:41.060
Chungseong! Love you!

76
03:41.060 --> 03:42.068
Been well?

77
03:42.068 --> 03:44.266
Have you been well?

78
03:46.190 --> 03:48.755
Staff Sergeant Choi Il Gu.

79
03:48.755 --> 03:50.582
I'm so glad you're back.

80
03:50.582 --> 03:52.398
I almost cried.

81
03:52.398 --> 03:55.303
You almost did, but you didn't, so quit being dramatic.

82
03:55.303 --> 03:57.529
I mean it.

83
03:57.529 --> 03:59.522
Ew, gross.

84
03:59.522 --> 04:01.361
Everything's fine except I have to watch

85
04:01.361 --> 04:04.203
Park Min Seok and Moon Bit Na Ri get discharged.

86
04:04.203 --> 04:07.002
Seeing him as a corporal already gets on my nerves.

87
04:07.002 --> 04:10.062
Corporal Park Min Seok! I've got some time under my belt now.

88
04:10.826 --> 04:13.529
But why did you really come back?

89
04:13.529 --> 04:15.068
Don't ask.

90
04:15.068 --> 04:18.239
I heard from the assistant platoon leader...

91
04:19.391 --> 04:21.246
Il Gu...

92
04:21.246 --> 04:25.515
Dad says I can only date a man whose job title ends in "sa" in Korean.

93
04:25.515 --> 04:27.776
Seriously?

94
04:27.776 --> 04:30.935
A job title ending in "sa"...

95
04:30.935 --> 04:33.128
Judge, prosecutor, lawyer.

96
04:33.128 --> 04:36.107
Not those, then doctor, pharmacist, Korean medicine doctor.

97
04:36.107 --> 04:37.734
A little late for those.

98
04:37.734 --> 04:41.442
Tax accountant, CPA, veterinarian...

99
04:41.442 --> 04:43.038
Those are out too.

100
04:43.038 --> 04:44.581
Wait!

101
04:44.581 --> 04:47.178
A job ending in "sa" I could actually do...

102
04:47.178 --> 04:48.836
Babe.

103
04:48.836 --> 04:50.916
There's one I can do.

104
04:50.916 --> 04:53.071
- What? - A job with "sa" in the title...

105
04:53.071 --> 04:54.402
- Ha-sa. - Ha-sa was the only one,

106
04:54.402 --> 04:56.481
so I heard that's why you became a staff sergeant?

107
04:56.481 --> 04:59.092
You're like the male lead in a drama.

108
04:59.092 --> 05:01.177
What a romantic.

109
05:01.177 --> 05:02.835
Is that true?

110
05:02.835 --> 05:04.374
You don't want to know.

111
05:04.374 --> 05:07.252
Duty's about to start,

112
05:07.252 --> 05:08.835
so get inside, soldiers.

113
05:08.835 --> 05:10.621
You really sound like a noncommissioned officer now.

114
05:10.621 --> 05:11.999
Knock it off.

115
05:11.999 --> 05:14.001
What, you think I'm a fake noncommissioned officer?

116
05:14.001 --> 05:16.077
Just tell us if it's true.

117
05:16.077 --> 05:17.723
Please.

118
05:17.723 --> 05:20.863
I'd really like you to go inside now, Sang Hun.

119
05:20.863 --> 05:22.190
But Staff Sergeant Choi Il Gu,

120
05:22.190 --> 05:23.493
did you have a girlfriend?

121
05:23.493 --> 05:25.604
You've never had one, right?

122
05:25.604 --> 05:27.899
Looks like you forgot what I'm like.

123
05:27.899 --> 05:29.552
If you don't want to die,

124
05:29.552 --> 05:31.736
shut up and get lost before you piss me off.

125
05:31.736 --> 05:33.615
- Why aren't you gone yet? - Yes.

126
05:33.615 --> 05:34.879
Huh?

127
05:34.879 --> 05:36.046
- You're not going? - Yes.

128
05:36.046 --> 05:38.171
Chungseong! Love you!

129
05:40.125 --> 05:44.096
Why he came back is still a mystery.

130
05:45.927 --> 05:48.934
Oh, and you know Jeon Se Gye? The really handsome guy.

131
05:48.934 --> 05:50.380
He's not that handsome.

132
05:50.380 --> 05:53.124
No, he's really handsome in person.

133
05:53.124 --> 05:55.814
- When it comes to looks... - Yeah.

134
06:03.381 --> 06:06.366
Are you all right?

135
06:08.816 --> 06:09.922
No.

136
06:09.922 --> 06:11.791
Anyway, you know him.

137
06:11.791 --> 06:13.348
He's a real soldier now.

138
06:13.348 --> 06:15.043
Your skin looks good lately.

139
06:15.043 --> 06:17.496
I told him to use a good face wash.

140
06:17.496 --> 06:18.617
Jeong Min's balding.

141
06:18.617 --> 06:21.200
My hair's just thin.

142
06:21.200 --> 06:23.842
Hey, check out his build.

143
06:25.206 --> 06:27.515
Oh, Jeon Sekai.

144
06:27.515 --> 06:30.739
Private First Class Jeon Sekai!

145
06:32.132 --> 06:33.659
You're a real soldier now, huh?

146
06:33.659 --> 06:35.477
You seem in a good mood today.

147
06:35.477 --> 06:38.503
Breakfast is sausage and vegetable stir-fry.

148
06:38.503 --> 06:40.287
I got chills.

149
06:40.287 --> 06:42.215
Our Se Gye's a real soldier now.

150
06:42.215 --> 06:43.219
Yes, that's right!

151
06:43.219 --> 06:45.745
Seeing Se Gye on television now is going to feel really weird.

152
06:45.745 --> 06:48.737
I'm happier and more at ease here.

153
06:54.540 --> 06:56.750
I'm starting to feel uncomfortable.

154
06:59.560 --> 07:00.931
Chungseong!

155
07:00.931 --> 07:02.455
Love you!

156
07:02.455 --> 07:03.845
Chungseong!

157
07:03.845 --> 07:04.929
Oh, our platoon leader.

158
07:04.929 --> 07:07.196
He got promoted to first lieutenant, and...

159
07:07.196 --> 07:09.025
My friend Private First Class Jeon Se Gye, you ready?

160
07:09.025 --> 07:10.644
I'll be leading you today.

161
07:10.644 --> 07:13.550
Private First Class Jeon Se Gye! I'll change and be right out.

162
07:13.550 --> 07:16.436
First Lieutenant Oh Seok Jin.

163
07:18.664 --> 07:21.233
First Lieutenant Oh Seok Jin!

164
07:21.882 --> 07:23.278
Since I was promoted to first lieutenant,

165
07:23.278 --> 07:24.574
has anyone asked about my mindset?

166
07:24.574 --> 07:25.362
Anyone?

167
07:25.362 --> 07:26.405
- No, sir. - No, sir.

168
07:26.405 --> 07:28.866
A first lieutenant is the second company-grade officer rank,

169
07:28.866 --> 07:31.182
which demands an even greater sense of responsibility and patriotism,

170
07:31.182 --> 07:34.237
while also requiring stronger communication between the company commander and the soldiers,

171
07:34.237 --> 07:36.581
as well as more efficient approaches to overall unit operations,

172
07:36.581 --> 07:38.267
with soldiers, noncommissioned officers, and junior officers...

173
07:38.267 --> 07:41.336
He talks even more than before.

174
07:42.056 --> 07:44.298
Oh, and Hyeon Uk.

175
07:44.298 --> 07:46.302
You know Hyeon Uk, my buddy from basic?

176
07:46.302 --> 07:49.819
I told you he ended up as a new recruit at our unit, right?

177
07:49.819 --> 07:53.902
Man, small world.

178
07:53.902 --> 07:57.663
The new-recruit prank when he arrived was incredible.

179
07:57.663 --> 07:59.521
Corporal Park Min Seok!

180
07:59.521 --> 08:01.517
I really want to do it.

181
08:01.517 --> 08:02.982
Min Seok.

182
08:02.982 --> 08:03.999
Don't volunteer.

183
08:03.999 --> 08:06.761
I know I can nail it this time.

184
08:06.761 --> 08:09.442
You can't do it since you know him.

185
08:09.442 --> 08:12.368
There's no point in the prank if you do it.

186
08:12.368 --> 08:14.037
Private First Class Moon Bit Na Ri!

187
08:14.037 --> 08:15.751
I can do it.

188
08:16.360 --> 08:18.302
I really can.

189
08:18.302 --> 08:20.572
Forget it, you...

190
08:21.401 --> 08:22.594
You don't have a kid, do you?

191
08:22.594 --> 08:23.545
Chungseong! Love you!

192
08:23.545 --> 08:24.908
Hey, need an actor?

193
08:24.908 --> 08:25.921
What do you mean, an actor?

194
08:25.921 --> 08:27.419
You're doing the new-recruit prank, aren't you?

195
08:27.419 --> 08:29.641
Why would a short-timer do a new-recruit prank?

196
08:29.641 --> 08:33.121
That's why, idiot, I can't do it once I'm out.

197
08:33.121 --> 08:34.653
So who's the star today?

198
08:34.653 --> 08:36.216
Private First Class Moon Bit Na Ri!

199
08:36.216 --> 08:37.708
All right, good luck.

200
08:37.708 --> 08:39.036
I know I can pull this off.

201
08:39.036 --> 08:40.871
Confidence, my ass...

202
08:42.773 --> 08:44.066
He's coming.

203
08:44.066 --> 08:45.356
Damn it, I don't know.

204
08:45.356 --> 08:46.453
Just get ready.

205
08:46.453 --> 08:48.575
- Hey, Bit Na Ri, come here. - Yes.

206
08:50.577 --> 08:51.656
Bit Na Ri, do it right.

207
08:51.656 --> 08:53.619
- Yes! - Keep your voice down, idiot.

208
08:53.619 --> 08:54.680
Yes.

209
08:54.680 --> 08:57.318
Hey, pull your collar up and loosen it a little.

210
08:57.318 --> 08:58.826
Okay.

211
08:58.826 --> 09:02.032
Hey, lie down. Back there.

212
09:02.032 --> 09:03.642
Yeah, lie down.

213
09:03.642 --> 09:05.195
Oh, good.

214
09:05.195 --> 09:08.398
- Hey, am I a private first class or a private? - You're a private. Fix your posture.

215
09:08.398 --> 09:10.857
Damn it, my back hurts.

216
09:15.223 --> 09:17.126
What's everyone doing?

217
09:17.126 --> 09:19.835
- Chungseong! Love you! - Yeah.

218
09:19.835 --> 09:21.576
Oh, man.

219
09:21.576 --> 09:22.948
Hey, the new guy's here.

220
09:22.948 --> 09:24.548
Come in.

221
09:46.013 --> 09:47.963
Unpack everything.

222
09:49.913 --> 09:53.260
Look at our new guy, all squared away.

223
09:53.260 --> 09:54.287
Choi Byeong Nam.

224
09:54.287 --> 09:55.566
Private Choi Byeong Nam!

225
09:55.566 --> 09:57.323
[EP01. Ace Recruit] That's what I like to hear.

226
09:57.323 --> 09:58.260
Thank you!

227
09:58.260 --> 10:00.713
Get his stuff unpacked and feed him.

228
10:00.713 --> 10:01.673
Yes.

229
10:01.673 --> 10:05.037
Don't be too hard on him just because he's new,

230
10:05.037 --> 10:07.865
and just act like you normally do.

231
10:07.865 --> 10:09.322
Moon Bit Na Ri...

232
10:09.322 --> 10:14.508
Sergeant.

233
10:14.508 --> 10:16.951
Sergeant Moon Bit Na Ri. Understood.

234
10:16.951 --> 10:18.490
Relax.

235
10:18.490 --> 10:21.330
- Chungseong! Love you! - At ease.

236
10:21.330 --> 10:23.678
- Good work. - Private Kim Hyeon Uk!

237
10:39.139 --> 10:40.248
Report in.

238
10:40.248 --> 10:42.403
Private Kim Hyeon Uk, reporting.

239
10:42.403 --> 10:44.072
I've been assigned to this unit.

240
10:44.072 --> 10:45.243
Reporting as ordered.

241
10:45.243 --> 10:47.933
Chungseong!

242
10:47.933 --> 10:49.049
Who said you could?

243
10:49.049 --> 10:50.161
I didn't hear you.

244
10:50.161 --> 10:52.589
I said, who told you you could transfer here?

245
10:52.589 --> 10:54.005
- I'm sorry! - Park Min Seok, down.

246
10:54.005 --> 10:56.532
Corporal Park Min Seok. Yes, down.

247
10:56.532 --> 10:57.680
You two were together in basic?

248
10:57.680 --> 10:59.283
Yes!

249
10:59.283 --> 11:01.383
- Hey. - Private Kim Hyeon Uk!

250
11:01.383 --> 11:02.895
Who said you could enlist twice?

251
11:02.895 --> 11:05.163
- I'm sorry! - Can't even keep track of your own juniors?

252
11:05.163 --> 11:06.223
I'm sorry.

253
11:06.223 --> 11:08.028
What have you been doing all this time?

254
11:08.028 --> 11:11.167
I was sick and spent a long time in the hospital.

255
11:11.167 --> 11:13.006
The hospital?

256
11:16.435 --> 11:18.762
Wait, what was wrong? Where did it hurt?

257
11:18.762 --> 11:21.821
Are you okay? How are you now?

258
11:21.821 --> 11:23.431
Im Da Hye, down.

259
11:23.431 --> 11:24.833
Uh, down.

260
11:24.833 --> 11:26.024
You can't even look after your junior's health?

261
11:26.024 --> 11:27.026
I'm sorry.

262
11:27.026 --> 11:27.771
Up.

263
11:27.771 --> 11:29.384
- Up. - Up.

264
11:29.384 --> 11:31.421
- Hey. - Private Kim Hyeon Uk!

265
11:31.421 --> 11:32.382
Do you have a girlfriend?

266
11:32.382 --> 11:33.720
- Yes. - Look at you.

267
11:33.720 --> 11:36.545
- Everyone, down. - Down.

268
11:36.545 --> 11:39.352
Your seniors don't even have girlfriends. A private gets to have one?

269
11:39.352 --> 11:40.608
Can't you manage your junior's love life?

270
11:40.608 --> 11:41.559
- I'm sorry. - I'm sorry.

271
11:41.559 --> 11:43.339
- Up. - Up.

272
11:43.339 --> 11:45.120
- Got an older sister? - No.

273
11:45.120 --> 11:47.506
- Everyone, down. - Down.

274
11:47.506 --> 11:48.954
Who said you could not have one?

275
11:48.954 --> 11:50.363
Can't you manage your junior's sisters?

276
11:50.363 --> 11:51.477
- I'm sorry. - I'm sorry.

277
11:51.477 --> 11:54.829
I don't have a sister, but I have lots of female friends.

278
11:54.829 --> 11:56.364
I'll ask them to visit.

279
11:56.364 --> 11:57.621
"Visit?"

280
11:58.384 --> 11:59.554
Really?

281
11:59.554 --> 12:00.860
- Yes. - Up.

282
12:00.860 --> 12:02.472
- Up. - Up.

283
12:03.914 --> 12:07.894
Sergeant Moon Bit Na Ri, ask him when they are...

284
12:07.894 --> 12:10.569
Can they really visit?

285
12:10.569 --> 12:11.914
Yes, they can.

286
12:11.914 --> 12:14.323
I'll call them today and set you up.

287
12:14.323 --> 12:15.995
Set us up?

288
12:20.032 --> 12:21.781
You're trying to win us

289
12:21.781 --> 12:23.916
over with dates, aren't you? Think I can't tell?

290
12:23.916 --> 12:25.615
- No, I'm serious. - Seriously?

291
12:25.615 --> 12:28.970
Who would you least want to set up?

292
12:29.865 --> 12:32.331
Three seconds. Pick one.

293
12:32.331 --> 12:33.351
One, two, three.

294
12:33.351 --> 12:35.141
I'm sorry!

295
12:38.986 --> 12:42.139
Mess up here, and your service is screwed.

296
12:42.139 --> 12:43.150
I'll ask again.

297
12:43.150 --> 12:45.270
Who's the ugliest guy here?

298
12:45.270 --> 12:48.200
Whose face got dragged across asphalt?

299
12:49.448 --> 12:50.577
One, two, three.

300
12:50.577 --> 12:52.177
I'm really sorry!

301
12:57.166 --> 13:00.421
Then who would you most want to set up?

302
13:00.421 --> 13:02.004
Pick one.

303
13:02.004 --> 13:03.392
One, two, three.

304
13:03.392 --> 13:06.396
You little jerk, are you messing with me?

305
13:06.396 --> 13:08.351
You said I was ugly.

306
13:08.351 --> 13:10.173
You said you didn't want to set me up!

307
13:10.173 --> 13:11.861
Are you messing with me?

308
13:11.861 --> 13:13.097
I'm sorry.

309
13:13.097 --> 13:15.343
I picked you as the one I'd least want to set up

310
13:15.343 --> 13:17.551
because the other guys might fight over who gets the date,

311
13:17.551 --> 13:19.726
and if you grew your hair out a little,

312
13:19.726 --> 13:21.251
you'd be the best-looking guy here.

313
13:21.251 --> 13:24.242
Plus, you're a sergeant and getting out soon,

314
13:24.242 --> 13:27.265
so it's the perfect time to set you up.

315
13:33.317 --> 13:36.965
Finally, a smart one.

316
13:36.965 --> 13:38.670
Reminds me of myself.

317
13:39.611 --> 13:41.263
- Oh, come on. - You laughing?

318
13:41.263 --> 13:42.403
- No. - I'm sorry.

319
13:42.403 --> 13:44.202
You think this is a joke?

320
13:44.860 --> 13:45.947
You here to have fun?

321
13:45.947 --> 13:47.618
Hey, Kim Sang Hun.

322
13:47.618 --> 13:48.986
Corporal Kim Sang Hun!

323
13:48.986 --> 13:51.322
Is being bad at soccer a crime?

324
13:51.322 --> 13:55.220
You can't cross. Why blame your junior?

325
13:55.220 --> 13:57.057
- Hey, Im Da Hye. - Corporal Im Da Hye!

326
13:57.057 --> 13:58.537
Why can't you answer properly?

327
13:58.537 --> 14:01.144
Answer faster!

328
14:01.144 --> 14:02.357
Right now!

329
14:02.357 --> 14:03.796
I'm sorry.

330
14:03.796 --> 14:04.803
Hey, Park Min Seok.

331
14:04.803 --> 14:06.024
Corporal Park Min Seok!

332
14:06.024 --> 14:08.555
You made corporal and now you own the army?

333
14:08.555 --> 14:11.808
The way you treat your juniors, you'd think you're a sergeant.

334
14:11.808 --> 14:13.409
What are you staring at?

335
14:13.409 --> 14:15.123
Think this is unfair?

336
14:15.123 --> 14:16.660
Look me in the eye.

337
14:16.660 --> 14:17.760
Choi Byeong Nam.

338
14:17.760 --> 14:18.952
Private Choi Byeong Nam!

339
14:18.952 --> 14:20.536
You're the biggest problem.

340
14:20.536 --> 14:23.349
What's with that face? Fix it.

341
14:23.349 --> 14:24.684
You can't read the room, can you?

342
14:24.684 --> 14:26.665
- Hey, new guy. - Private Kim Hyeon Uk!

343
14:26.665 --> 14:30.104
I'll show you what happens when a private can't read the room.

344
14:30.104 --> 14:32.584
Choi Byeong Nam, everyone above you and below me,

345
14:32.584 --> 14:35.583
fall in!

346
14:36.638 --> 14:38.436
We're already here!

347
14:38.436 --> 14:41.173
- Hey, jerk. - You don't know your place, do you?

348
14:41.173 --> 14:42.815
You jerk!

349
14:49.497 --> 14:52.034
He's playing all the seniors,

350
14:52.034 --> 14:53.801
and it turns out...

351
14:56.431 --> 14:58.883
Old physical training uniform.

352
14:58.883 --> 15:00.860
At least a sergeant.

353
15:00.860 --> 15:03.528
Shiny dog tags. Brand-new slippers.

354
15:03.528 --> 15:04.584
Okay.

355
15:04.584 --> 15:07.314
Worn-out physical training uniform over there too.

356
15:07.314 --> 15:08.886
Okay.

357
15:08.886 --> 15:10.534
Pathetic.

358
15:11.793 --> 15:15.153
His instincts were unreal.

359
15:15.153 --> 15:18.537
So the whole new-recruit prank was a bust.

360
15:18.537 --> 15:20.494
It was way more fun when I did it.

361
15:20.494 --> 15:24.270
Moon Bit Na Ri, though... His delivery was off, and he couldn't act.

362
15:24.270 --> 15:28.476
That's experience and instincts for you.

363
15:29.210 --> 15:32.557
Right after he transferred in, Corporal Jeong Gyu Seon picked a fight,

364
15:32.557 --> 15:33.921
and things blew up.

365
15:33.921 --> 15:36.072
Corporal Jeong Gyu Seon even got sent to the guardhouse.

366
15:36.072 --> 15:37.671
His service almost went south,

367
15:37.671 --> 15:39.848
but then he met me, and things turned around.

368
15:39.848 --> 15:42.609
What else did I teach Hyeon Uk...

369
15:42.609 --> 15:43.965
Huh!

370
15:46.079 --> 15:48.965
Oh! You scared me.

371
15:48.965 --> 15:51.025
What? We're not there yet.

372
15:51.025 --> 15:52.703
Can you open the door?

373
15:52.703 --> 15:54.913
The door? Why?

374
15:54.913 --> 15:56.927
Three, two...

375
15:56.927 --> 15:58.791
Uh, okay.

376
16:05.008 --> 16:07.290
You...

377
16:07.290 --> 16:08.698
talk too much.

378
16:08.698 --> 16:10.082
Huh?

379
16:12.788 --> 16:14.517
Hey!

380
16:14.517 --> 16:16.225
Where are you going?

381
16:16.225 --> 16:19.574
Hey, Park Min Ju!

382
16:19.574 --> 16:22.357
She's seriously psycho.

383
16:25.860 --> 16:27.777
Hey, Park Min Ju!

384
16:27.777 --> 16:30.722
What am I supposed to do alone?

385
16:30.722 --> 16:31.908
Hey!

386
16:31.908 --> 16:34.149
[May this youth shine for the motherland!] Hey!

387
16:35.972 --> 16:38.429
Oh, I'm finally here.

388
16:38.429 --> 16:40.253
Seriously.

389
16:40.253 --> 16:41.707
Park Min Ju...

390
16:41.707 --> 16:43.461
I hope your dog tags give you a rash.

391
16:43.461 --> 16:48.031
I hope you get an ingrown toenail and cellulitis too, Park Min Ju.

392
16:48.031 --> 16:49.331
What a life.

393
16:49.331 --> 16:51.212
Stop! Hands up! Move, and I'll shoot!

394
16:51.212 --> 16:53.231
Go ahead. Shoot me.

395
16:53.231 --> 16:55.256
- Hey, Park Min Seok. Good leave? - Yeah.

396
16:55.256 --> 16:57.471
Who's guard commander today?

397
17:00.553 --> 17:02.312
Me, asshole.

398
17:02.312 --> 17:03.797
Chungseong! Love you!

399
17:03.797 --> 17:05.906
What happened? You ran here in this heat?

400
17:05.906 --> 17:08.505
Yeah. Something came up.

401
17:08.505 --> 17:11.253
You barely even walk.

402
17:11.253 --> 17:14.083
What, did the heat get to you?

403
17:14.083 --> 17:15.344
Get inside and report in.

404
17:15.344 --> 17:16.895
Yes. Understood. Good work.

405
17:16.895 --> 17:18.746
Chungseong! Love you!

406
17:20.079 --> 17:22.625
Wait.

407
17:23.837 --> 17:26.418
That thing in your hand looks suspicious.

408
17:26.418 --> 17:29.918
I just bought it to mix with milk.

409
17:29.918 --> 17:31.460
This is Park Min Seok we're talking about.

410
17:31.460 --> 17:33.685
On his first leave, we told him to sneak in Maxim,

411
17:33.685 --> 17:37.018
and the legend brought in Maxim coffee instead.

412
17:37.018 --> 17:38.718
Oh, I remember.

413
17:38.718 --> 17:40.462
I should've killed you then.

414
17:40.462 --> 17:43.414
I spared you because I was busy. Look where that got me.

415
17:43.414 --> 17:46.231
That was ages ago. I don't do that anymore.

416
17:46.231 --> 17:47.836
Oh? So this time

417
17:47.836 --> 17:49.983
you hid it better?

418
17:49.983 --> 17:52.669
No...

419
17:52.669 --> 17:54.016
Open it.

420
17:54.016 --> 17:55.058
I didn't hear you.

421
17:55.058 --> 17:57.134
Min Seok, don't forget.

422
17:57.134 --> 17:59.482
I'm Choi Il Gu.

423
18:00.660 --> 18:03.000
You learned all this from me.

424
18:03.000 --> 18:06.638
Why's this opening so easily? It's new.

425
18:09.026 --> 18:10.920
Hey, the new issue.

426
18:10.920 --> 18:12.842
This was sold out. How'd you get it?

427
18:12.842 --> 18:14.859
Staff Sergeant Choi Il Gu, please. Just this once.

428
18:14.859 --> 18:16.400
This was really hard to get.

429
18:16.400 --> 18:18.046
This is insane.

430
18:18.046 --> 18:20.032
Don't tear it! No...

431
18:22.894 --> 18:25.187
Don't blame me, okay?

432
18:25.187 --> 18:27.283
I'm just doing my job.

433
18:27.283 --> 18:28.998
Hey, this...

434
18:30.090 --> 18:31.819
Damn it.

435
18:33.158 --> 18:34.865
Hey, Park Min Seok.

436
18:34.865 --> 18:36.205
Corporal Park Min Seok!

437
18:36.205 --> 18:37.444
Wipe that look off your face.

438
18:37.444 --> 18:38.958
This is just my face.

439
18:38.958 --> 18:41.315
You made corporal and now you don't even hide that look?

440
18:41.315 --> 18:42.361
Want me to call a formation?

441
18:42.361 --> 18:44.286
Think I can't now that I'm a staff sergeant?

442
18:44.286 --> 18:46.867
No. I'm sorry.

443
18:46.867 --> 18:49.284
Get lost.

444
18:49.284 --> 18:51.088
Yes. Understood.

445
18:51.861 --> 18:53.680
- This is plastic, so... - Yes. Understood.

446
18:53.680 --> 18:55.038
- This one's paper, so it goes here. - Yes.

447
18:55.038 --> 18:57.483
Park Min Seok isn't bringing coffee again, is he?

448
18:57.483 --> 18:58.935
Just trust him.

449
18:58.935 --> 19:01.015
Why's he taking so long?

450
19:02.962 --> 19:05.926
Corporal Park Min Seok, back from leave.

451
19:05.926 --> 19:07.397
Hey, what happened?

452
19:07.397 --> 19:09.729
Min Seok, did it work?

453
19:09.729 --> 19:11.942
Uh, well...

454
19:16.927 --> 19:18.966
They ripped out all the photos.

455
19:21.585 --> 19:22.658
I'm sorry.

456
19:22.658 --> 19:24.724
Still, good work. Go unpack.

457
19:24.724 --> 19:26.148
Yes. Understood.

458
19:26.148 --> 19:27.219
Good work.

459
19:27.219 --> 19:29.650
Couldn't even sneak one thing in?

460
19:29.650 --> 19:31.216
- Throw this out. - Yes. Understood.

461
19:31.216 --> 19:32.931
Never ask that guy to do anything.

462
19:32.931 --> 19:35.115
- Paper goes here. - Ah, yes.

463
19:35.115 --> 19:37.354
- Sergeant Kim Sang Hun. - What?

464
19:37.354 --> 19:40.498
Staff Sergeant Choi Il Gu said to give you this...

465
19:40.498 --> 19:42.098
What is it?

466
19:48.816 --> 19:50.792
Hey, Park Min Seok.

467
19:50.792 --> 19:51.738
Corporal Park Min Seok!

468
19:51.738 --> 19:54.209
What's with that tone?

469
19:54.209 --> 19:55.399
No.

470
19:55.399 --> 19:58.308
Throw this out on your way.

471
19:58.308 --> 20:00.284
Yes. Understood.

472
20:00.284 --> 20:02.201
Recycle it properly.

473
20:04.168 --> 20:05.461
Huh?

474
20:06.657 --> 20:08.841
Sergeant Choi Il Gu... Oh, Staff Sergeant Choi Il Gu!

475
20:08.841 --> 20:10.493
Thank you so much. I love you.

476
20:10.493 --> 20:12.284
Chungseong! I love you!

477
20:12.284 --> 20:13.460
- Ugh, gross. - Thank you!

478
20:13.460 --> 20:15.398
Only when you need something.

479
20:18.976 --> 20:20.568
- Did it work? - It worked.

480
20:20.568 --> 20:22.039
Nice! You did it!

481
20:22.039 --> 20:23.799
Corporal Park Ik Jeom!

482
20:23.799 --> 20:25.629
Park Ik Jeom, good work.

483
20:25.629 --> 20:26.905
- Well done! - Thank you!

484
20:26.905 --> 20:28.595
- Staff Sergeant Choi Il Gu. - Well done!

485
20:28.595 --> 20:29.934
- Thank you. - Hey.

486
20:29.934 --> 20:31.803
- Yes. - Hyeon Uk, keep watch.

487
20:31.803 --> 20:33.461
Everyone, get over here.

488
20:33.461 --> 20:35.061
Yes. Understood.

489
20:42.033 --> 20:44.034
The next one's even crazier.

490
20:44.034 --> 20:44.995
Oh, yeah?

491
20:44.995 --> 20:47.302
- Careful. Don't tear it. - Okay.

492
20:47.302 --> 20:48.826
- You're burning up. - Private First Class Moon Bit Na Ri.

493
20:48.826 --> 20:50.151
Shut up.

494
20:50.151 --> 20:51.427
You're keeping watch, right?

495
20:51.427 --> 20:53.669
What? Yes.

496
21:13.350 --> 21:15.423
Oh, that was sold out.

497
21:15.423 --> 21:18.398
Yeah. It was really hard to find.

498
21:18.398 --> 21:19.533
Nice job.

499
21:19.533 --> 21:21.415
Thank you...

500
21:29.148 --> 21:30.841
Company Commander! Chungseong! Love you!

501
21:30.841 --> 21:32.049
Yeah. Love you too.

502
21:32.049 --> 21:33.110
Love you.

503
21:33.110 --> 21:36.012
I was wondering what you guys were doing in this heat.

504
21:36.012 --> 21:38.698
What a lovely sight.

505
21:38.698 --> 21:41.703
How could you not like this?

506
21:41.703 --> 21:43.213
Park Min Seok.

507
21:43.213 --> 21:44.146
Corporal Park Min Seok!

508
21:44.146 --> 21:46.056
You bought this coming back from leave?

509
21:46.056 --> 21:47.503
Yes.

510
21:47.503 --> 21:49.208
Nobody told you to, right?

511
21:49.208 --> 21:52.517
Uh, well, yes...

512
21:52.517 --> 21:54.117
Everyone, close your eyes.

513
21:55.286 --> 21:59.008
Anyone who told or asked him to bring something, raise your hand.

514
21:59.008 --> 22:00.367
Wait.

515
22:00.367 --> 22:04.029
Corporal Im Da Hye will definitely raise his hand.

516
22:04.029 --> 22:06.367
What if I raise mine too?

517
22:13.392 --> 22:14.992
Everyone, open your eyes.

518
22:16.968 --> 22:18.568
Hands down.

519
22:19.191 --> 22:20.438
I see.

520
22:20.438 --> 22:22.430
Comrades don't turn their backs on each other

521
22:22.430 --> 22:24.034
even when things get desperate.

522
22:24.034 --> 22:26.073
That's the right thing to do.

523
22:26.073 --> 22:28.784
Good to see you looking out for each other.

524
22:28.784 --> 22:31.409
I'll let this slide.

525
22:31.409 --> 22:33.519
Pass!

526
22:35.656 --> 22:36.695
Park Min Seok.

527
22:36.695 --> 22:38.718
Corporal Park Min Seok!

528
22:38.718 --> 22:40.380
Love you.

529
22:40.380 --> 22:42.904
Chungseong! Love you too!

530
22:46.387 --> 22:48.927
Thanks, Park Min Seok.

531
22:48.927 --> 22:50.312
I won't forget this.

532
22:50.312 --> 22:52.757
- Chungseong! - Corporal Park Min Seok.

533
22:52.757 --> 22:56.027
Thanks, Min Seok.

534
22:56.027 --> 22:57.697
That's what they'll say, right?

535
22:57.697 --> 23:01.577
I see. Good to see you taking responsibility as a senior.

536
23:01.577 --> 23:03.524
Park Min Seok, hand down.

537
23:06.402 --> 23:08.270
Huh?

538
23:08.270 --> 23:09.454
Corporal Im Da Hye...

539
23:09.454 --> 23:10.629
Park Min Seok.

540
23:10.629 --> 23:11.638
Corporal Park Min Seok!

541
23:11.638 --> 23:12.936
To the admin office.

542
23:12.936 --> 23:14.294
Why is that?

543
23:14.294 --> 23:15.821
Only you raised your hand.

544
23:15.821 --> 23:17.587
No, uh...

545
23:17.587 --> 23:20.218
I like your honesty.

546
23:20.218 --> 23:21.780
Let's go.

547
23:21.780 --> 23:22.826
Corporal Im Da Hye...

548
23:22.826 --> 23:23.869
Thanks.

549
23:23.869 --> 23:24.872
Sergeant Kim Sang Hun...

550
23:24.872 --> 23:27.323
- Good luck. - Wait.

551
23:28.382 --> 23:30.902
But who tore this up before giving it to you?

552
23:30.902 --> 23:32.341
Well...

553
23:35.045 --> 23:37.255
Come on, let's go.

554
23:37.255 --> 23:39.059
I'm sorry.

555
23:46.211 --> 23:47.896
Chungseong! Love you!

556
23:47.896 --> 23:49.951
- Hey. - Yes, sir!

557
23:49.951 --> 23:51.397
Where's Park Min Seok?

558
23:51.397 --> 23:53.298
Do you mean Min Seok?

559
23:53.298 --> 23:55.772
- Earlier, he... - Hey, go tell him.

560
23:55.772 --> 23:58.794
Tell him to desert if he doesn't want to die. If he wants to live, tell him to desert.

561
23:58.794 --> 24:00.802
So I should just tell him to desert?

562
24:00.802 --> 24:04.109
Yeah, before I tear him apart like that magazine.

563
24:07.694 --> 24:09.191
Are you okay?

564
24:09.191 --> 24:11.938
Corporal Park Min Seok, are you okay?

565
24:11.938 --> 24:13.992
Yeah, I'm fine.

566
24:13.992 --> 24:17.484
Corporal Park Min Seok. I just came back from hell.

567
24:17.484 --> 24:20.510
Staff Sergeant Choi Il Gu has really changed.

568
24:20.510 --> 24:23.044
I seriously almost died in there.

569
24:23.044 --> 24:24.881
That was rough, Min Seok.

570
24:24.881 --> 24:28.402
Still, I got off pretty easy.

571
24:29.300 --> 24:30.939
Hyeon Uk, did you polish your combat boots?

572
24:30.939 --> 24:32.357
Private Kim Hyeon Uk. Not yet.

573
24:32.357 --> 24:33.372
Then let's hurry.

574
24:33.372 --> 24:34.974
Yes, understood.

575
24:40.294 --> 24:41.840
Hey, thanks.

576
24:41.840 --> 24:43.778
I'll go polish my boots with Hyeon Uk and be right back.

577
24:43.778 --> 24:45.068
Go ahead.

578
24:45.068 --> 24:46.808
- Want me to help you walk? - No, I'm good.

579
24:46.808 --> 24:48.356
Yes, I'll be back.

580
24:48.356 --> 24:51.415
- Hurry back. - Come on, let's go.

581
24:51.415 --> 24:53.189
- Hey, Bit Na Ri. - Private First Class Moon Bit Na Ri.

582
24:53.189 --> 24:54.834
If anything happens, come get us right away.

583
24:54.834 --> 24:56.655
Understood.

584
24:56.655 --> 25:00.153
Park Min Seok really screwed up this time.

585
25:01.166 --> 25:03.456
Have you heard about the new battalion commander?

586
25:03.456 --> 25:06.411
Yes. The rumors are everywhere. I heard someone famous is coming.

587
25:06.411 --> 25:08.931
Yeah, he's even in the military newspaper.

588
25:08.931 --> 25:10.877
He doesn't seem like an ordinary guy.

589
25:10.877 --> 25:13.147
[Byeon Hyeok Jin, leading the way in modernizing military barracks culture]

590
25:13.147 --> 25:16.620
By the way, have you seen the hot new issue?

591
25:16.620 --> 25:18.991
No, I'm good.

592
25:18.991 --> 25:20.492
Come on, it's just us.

593
25:20.492 --> 25:21.971
I heard it sold out.

594
25:21.971 --> 25:23.208
I said I'm good.

595
25:23.208 --> 25:25.518
I won't tell your wife. Just take a peek.

596
25:25.518 --> 25:27.778
I already saw it.

597
25:30.953 --> 25:32.273
Here, look at this instead.

598
25:32.273 --> 25:34.059
Yes, sure.

599
25:37.203 --> 25:40.548
[Byeon Hyeok Jin, leading the way in modernizing military barracks culture]

600
25:40.548 --> 25:44.460
Man, how is it still this hot at night?

601
25:46.343 --> 25:49.276
- Here you go. - Thanks.

602
25:54.137 --> 25:56.289
- Corporal Park Min Seok. - Yeah?

603
25:56.289 --> 25:59.090
I'm sorry. I should've kept a better lookout earlier.

604
25:59.090 --> 26:00.146
Oh, that?

605
26:00.146 --> 26:01.673
It's fine. Don't worry about it.

606
26:01.673 --> 26:03.352
I'm just glad it worked out okay.

607
26:03.352 --> 26:06.740
Yeah. I got off easy because I usually behave myself.

608
26:06.740 --> 26:08.351
Yes, that's true.

609
26:08.351 --> 26:10.172
Nothing happened while I was on leave, right?

610
26:10.172 --> 26:11.827
No, nothing.

611
26:13.947 --> 26:18.287
Being here with just you suddenly reminds me of basic training.

612
26:19.793 --> 26:23.015
[2nd Platoon]

613
26:23.734 --> 26:27.083
All right, get your issued gear organized. Quickly.

614
26:27.083 --> 26:29.088
- Yes, understood. - Yes, understood.

615
26:31.836 --> 26:33.888
What's with you? Where are your slippers?

616
26:33.888 --> 26:34.976
What are you doing? Hurry up.

617
26:34.976 --> 26:37.224
Huh? Well...

618
26:37.224 --> 26:38.337
Is something wrong?

619
26:38.337 --> 26:41.259
I think they gave me the wrong size. My feet really hurt.

620
26:41.259 --> 26:42.488
What?

621
26:42.488 --> 26:45.017
- You should've said something. - It's fine.

622
26:45.017 --> 26:47.117
I was afraid I'd get yelled at.

623
26:47.117 --> 26:50.145
Trainee 11, Kim Hyeon Uk. I have a question, Drill Instructor.

624
26:50.145 --> 26:51.767
What is it? We don't have time. Make it quick.

625
26:51.767 --> 26:53.892
My fellow trainee got the wrong size combat boots.

626
26:53.892 --> 26:56.269
Can he exchange them?

627
26:56.269 --> 26:58.430
Why are you asking for him?

628
26:58.430 --> 27:00.035
I'm sorry!

629
27:00.696 --> 27:01.773
We'll exchange them later.

630
27:01.773 --> 27:04.373
For now, get everything organized. Got it?

631
27:04.373 --> 27:06.380
Trainee 12, Park Min Seok.

632
27:06.380 --> 27:08.101
Yes, understood. Thank you.

633
27:08.101 --> 27:10.735
If the guy next to you has something you don't,

634
27:10.735 --> 27:12.199
- Thank you. - raise your hand and tell me now.

635
27:12.199 --> 27:14.532
There will be no exchanges after this. Got it?

636
27:14.532 --> 27:16.764
- Yes, understood. - Yes, understood.

637
27:16.764 --> 27:18.256
If it weren't for you back then,

638
27:18.256 --> 27:20.639
I'd probably still be wearing those tiny boots.

639
27:21.387 --> 27:23.809
Those were the days, huh?

640
27:24.993 --> 27:26.503
Yes, they were.

641
27:29.633 --> 27:32.145
Jeong Min, you are definitely going bald.

642
27:32.145 --> 27:33.409
- And there's no cure for baldness. - Chungseong! Love you!

643
27:33.409 --> 27:35.704
- Oh, Park Min Seok. - Corporal Park Min Seok.

644
27:35.704 --> 27:36.838
Have a good leave?

645
27:36.838 --> 27:38.055
Yes, I did.

646
27:38.055 --> 27:39.190
What did you do while you were out?

647
27:39.190 --> 27:41.061
What do you think? I practically lived at the club.

648
27:41.061 --> 27:42.810
Cut the crap.

649
27:42.810 --> 27:43.817
I'm serious.

650
27:43.817 --> 27:45.357
You practically lived at an internet cafe.

651
27:45.357 --> 27:46.717
How did you know?

652
27:46.717 --> 27:48.836
It's obvious.

653
27:48.836 --> 27:51.140
- Oh, Kim Hyeon Uk. - Private Kim Hyeon Uk.

654
27:51.140 --> 27:53.337
I've been hearing a lot about you lately.

655
27:53.337 --> 27:54.479
I'm sorry. I didn't hear you.

656
27:54.479 --> 27:56.042
What have you been hearing?

657
27:56.042 --> 27:58.678
That he's killing it.

658
27:58.678 --> 27:59.795
Thank you.

659
27:59.795 --> 28:02.640
I used to be called an ace too.

660
28:02.640 --> 28:04.330
You've got Sergeant Cha Hoon's athleticism,

661
28:04.330 --> 28:05.842
Sergeant Kim Sang Hun's soccer skills,

662
28:05.842 --> 28:07.533
and Sergeant Shim Jin Woo's instincts.

663
28:07.533 --> 28:08.827
Private Kim Hyeon Uk.

664
28:08.827 --> 28:10.757
I'm flattered.

665
28:10.757 --> 28:12.810
See? This kid really is something else.

666
28:12.810 --> 28:16.257
But when it comes to instincts, don't I take the prize?

667
28:17.630 --> 28:19.300
Should I rub shoe polish on your head?

668
28:19.300 --> 28:21.966
Excuse me, gentlemen?

669
28:22.862 --> 28:25.036
I'm sorry.

670
28:25.036 --> 28:26.884
- Hey, Hyeon Uk. - Private Kim Hyeon Uk.

671
28:26.884 --> 28:28.624
- How are you holding up? - I'm doing well.

672
28:28.624 --> 28:30.448
Corporal Im Da Hye takes good care of me,

673
28:30.448 --> 28:32.329
and Corporal Park Min Seok teaches me a lot.

674
28:32.927 --> 28:34.143
You even know the proper rank etiquette.

675
28:34.143 --> 28:35.596
You really know how to survive in the army.

676
28:35.596 --> 28:38.565
- Thank you! - I taught him that too.

677
28:38.565 --> 28:40.414
Look at you.

678
28:41.240 --> 28:42.898
- Oh, right. Corporal Kim Dong Woo. - Yeah?

679
28:42.898 --> 28:44.684
Have you heard the rumors about the new battalion commander?

680
28:44.684 --> 28:45.975
What rumors?

681
28:45.975 --> 28:48.481
[Battalion Commander's Office]

682
28:52.060 --> 28:54.789
Corporal Sung Yoon Mo, reporting to the battalion commander's office.

683
28:54.789 --> 28:57.236
May I enter?

684
29:01.576 --> 29:03.284
No one's here.

685
29:07.120 --> 29:09.014
[Award Certificate]

686
29:09.014 --> 29:11.392
They say he's a total hotshot.

687
29:11.392 --> 29:12.527
Every promotion on the first try.

688
29:12.527 --> 29:13.969
I heard it from Yoon Mo too.

689
29:13.969 --> 29:15.605
Apparently, he's seriously intimidating.

690
29:15.605 --> 29:17.551
Really?

691
29:17.551 --> 29:20.851
I've got a bad feeling about this.

692
29:20.851 --> 29:22.553
Things are about to get rough.

693
29:25.098 --> 29:29.283
[Battalion Commander: Lieutenant Colonel Byeon Hyeok Jin]

694
29:32.067 --> 29:33.672
Attention, barracks.

695
29:33.672 --> 29:35.254
All personnel, lights out.

696
29:35.254 --> 29:37.063
Good night.

697
29:41.756 --> 29:43.311
Hyeon Uk.

698
29:43.311 --> 29:44.359
Hyeon Uk.

699
29:44.359 --> 29:46.076
Shh.

700
29:47.329 --> 29:49.204
Come out.

701
29:49.204 --> 29:51.041
Yes, understood.

702
29:52.499 --> 29:54.696
- Ta-da! - Thank you.

703
29:54.696 --> 29:55.836
Remember bag ramen?

704
29:55.836 --> 29:57.870
Back in basic, we'd always watch the instructors eat it

705
29:57.870 --> 29:59.188
and wish we could have some.

706
29:59.188 --> 30:00.788
Yes, I remember.

707
30:04.495 --> 30:06.449
You know something?

708
30:06.449 --> 30:08.293
You're the ace of our company.

709
30:08.293 --> 30:10.351
No, I'm not!

710
30:10.351 --> 30:12.388
- Hyeon Uk. - Private Kim Hyeon Uk.

711
30:12.388 --> 30:16.717
When it's just us, drop the formalities. We went through basic training together.

712
30:16.717 --> 30:19.269
- I can't! - Seriously, relax. It's fine.

713
30:19.269 --> 30:21.445
Come on. Just try it once.

714
30:21.445 --> 30:22.751
Hope your shift's going well.

715
30:22.751 --> 30:25.008
You're looking out for Hyeon Uk again?

716
30:25.008 --> 30:27.284
You've never made bag ramen for me. Not once.

717
30:27.284 --> 30:29.781
Come on. What, are you jealous?

718
30:31.322 --> 30:32.663
Good work out there.

719
30:32.663 --> 30:33.726
Chungseong.

720
30:33.726 --> 30:35.009
Love you.

721
30:35.009 --> 30:36.291
Jeon Se Gye.

722
30:36.291 --> 30:37.808
Take a seat.

723
30:37.808 --> 30:40.081
Hey, Se Gye.

724
30:40.081 --> 30:42.245
Is it okay to eat like this at night? You'll gain weight.

725
30:42.245 --> 30:44.500
I'll lose it when I get out.

726
30:44.500 --> 30:47.037
Doesn't food taste best after duty?

727
30:47.037 --> 30:48.503
Yeah, it does.

728
30:48.503 --> 30:50.872
It really does taste best after duty.

729
30:50.872 --> 30:53.222
You're a real soldier now, huh?

730
30:53.222 --> 30:55.948
Private First Class Jeon Se Gye.

731
30:55.948 --> 30:57.953
Why are you having rice noodles?

732
30:57.953 --> 30:59.309
Want my Shin Ramen?

733
30:59.309 --> 31:01.521
No, thank you. I like these.

734
31:01.521 --> 31:04.990
These rice noodles have a flavor you can't get on the outside.

735
31:04.990 --> 31:07.866
At this rate, you'll land a rice noodle commercial.

736
31:07.866 --> 31:10.670
"The taste of deployment. Rice noodles."

737
31:10.670 --> 31:12.975
He said, "The taste of deployment."

738
31:12.975 --> 31:14.319
- All right, eat up. - Thank you.

739
31:14.319 --> 31:16.551
- Let's eat, Hyeon Uk. - Yes.

740
31:16.551 --> 31:18.432
Excuse me, Corporal Park Min Seok?

741
31:18.432 --> 31:20.105
- Yeah? - Could I have a bite?

742
31:20.105 --> 31:22.189
- You think I'd let you? - Please, just one bite.

743
31:22.189 --> 31:23.462
Eat after your shift.

744
31:23.462 --> 31:24.554
Please, just one bite.

745
31:24.554 --> 31:26.906
- What? - Just one bite.

746
31:26.906 --> 31:27.989
Seriously.

747
31:27.989 --> 31:30.514
Come on, that's too much.

748
31:30.514 --> 31:32.004
Hey, Jeon Se Gye.

749
31:32.004 --> 31:34.749
Come on.

750
31:34.749 --> 31:36.437
- Have mine instead... - Hyeon Uk, spit in yours too. Hurry.

751
31:36.437 --> 31:37.246
Hey.

752
31:37.246 --> 31:38.786
Hurry up and spit in it. Spit in it now.

753
31:38.786 --> 31:40.872
- Spit in it. - Hurry.

754
31:42.638 --> 31:44.557
- I'm sorry. - Eat after your shift.

755
31:44.557 --> 31:45.510
You can have mine.

756
31:45.510 --> 31:46.959
I don't want it.

757
31:46.959 --> 31:48.441
Thank you. Hope your shift's going well.

758
31:48.441 --> 31:49.761
Enjoy.

759
31:49.761 --> 31:51.259
Hope your shift's going well.

760
31:56.892 --> 31:58.835
You're really enjoying that.

761
32:00.865 --> 32:02.754
Man, I'm so full.

762
32:03.589 --> 32:04.656
Thank you. I really enjoyed it.

763
32:04.656 --> 32:06.662
Look at my stomach.

764
32:07.331 --> 32:09.469
- Have you ever had cream udon? - No, not yet.

765
32:09.469 --> 32:11.202
I'll make you cream udon next time.

766
32:11.202 --> 32:12.896
Understood.

767
32:12.896 --> 32:15.026
- Corporal Park Min Seok, could I... - Yeah?

768
32:15.026 --> 32:17.130
Could I use the bathroom real quick?

769
32:17.130 --> 32:18.136
Yeah, go ahead.

770
32:18.136 --> 32:20.022
- Thank you. - Sure.

771
32:20.912 --> 32:22.524
Man, I'm full.

772
32:57.910 --> 32:59.937
Damn it.

773
33:06.069 --> 33:07.868
The heat wave continues this week...

774
33:07.868 --> 33:10.423
- What did they say we're doing this morning? - Highs will reach 33 degrees,

775
33:10.423 --> 33:13.324
with a feels-like temperature above 35.

776
33:13.324 --> 33:15.632
Be sure to take care of yourselves

777
33:15.632 --> 33:17.870
to prevent heat-related illnesses.

778
33:17.870 --> 33:20.277
Especially in the afternoon...

779
33:20.277 --> 33:21.560
We're cleaning out the supply warehouse,

780
33:21.560 --> 33:23.699
so make sure you bring your boonie hats and gloves.

781
33:23.699 --> 33:26.301
Okay, good call, rookie.

782
33:26.301 --> 33:28.882
Private Kim Hyeon Uk. Thank you!

783
33:31.218 --> 33:32.394
Guys.

784
33:32.394 --> 33:34.920
Don't slack off just because it's hot. Stay sharp on duty.

785
33:34.920 --> 33:36.223
- Understood. - Understood.

786
33:36.223 --> 33:38.252
[May this youth shine for the motherland!]

787
33:40.081 --> 33:41.268
Chungseong! Love you!

788
33:41.268 --> 33:42.508
Hey, what's the temperature today?

789
33:42.508 --> 33:45.047
31 degrees.

790
33:45.047 --> 33:46.776
It's September, a whole month past the start of fall.

791
33:46.776 --> 33:48.235
How can it still be this hot?

792
33:48.235 --> 33:50.274
It feels even hotter here than on the outside.

793
33:50.274 --> 33:51.911
Weather's a funny thing.

794
33:51.911 --> 33:55.179
The second you get on base, it's hot, then hotter.

795
33:55.179 --> 33:57.927
How can it be this hot?

796
34:01.704 --> 34:03.250
It's hot.

797
34:03.250 --> 34:05.560
Hey, why aren't you outside?

798
34:06.535 --> 34:09.422
Looks brutal out there.

799
34:09.422 --> 34:10.947
We are in for a long day.

800
34:10.947 --> 34:12.648
Our country has four seasons.

801
34:12.648 --> 34:14.508
Why does the army only have two?

802
34:14.508 --> 34:15.711
Cold and hot.

803
34:15.711 --> 34:17.687
It does have four.

804
34:17.687 --> 34:19.270
Hot, freaking hot,

805
34:19.270 --> 34:22.014
cold, freaking cold.

806
34:22.014 --> 34:23.240
Hey, Choi Il Gu.

807
34:23.240 --> 34:24.810
Why aren't you guys outside?

808
34:24.810 --> 34:27.242
We were checking the headcount.

809
34:27.242 --> 34:29.204
Are you one of them now?

810
34:29.204 --> 34:30.322
Get outside!

811
34:30.322 --> 34:32.759
- Come on, get out. Hurry. - Understood.

812
34:32.759 --> 34:34.249
Drink plenty of water while you work.

813
34:34.249 --> 34:36.375
- Understood. - Understood.

814
34:45.080 --> 34:46.595
It's hot. Let's get this done fast.

815
34:46.595 --> 34:47.841
- Understood. - Understood.

816
34:47.841 --> 34:50.020
Choi Byeong Nam, why are you resting here?

817
34:50.020 --> 34:52.155
They say short-timers should watch out for falling leaves.

818
34:52.155 --> 34:53.522
Man, you've lost it.

819
34:53.522 --> 34:55.028
Watch out. A leaf's falling.

820
34:55.028 --> 34:57.790
Come on, let's get this done. Hurry.

821
34:57.790 --> 34:59.548
Se Gye, help Bit Na Ri.

822
34:59.548 --> 35:01.421
- Understood. - Go with him, man.

823
35:01.421 --> 35:02.484
Understood.

824
35:02.484 --> 35:04.369
This is heavy.

825
35:08.635 --> 35:09.852
Make sure you drink some water.

826
35:09.852 --> 35:11.598
I'll move this up first, then drink.

827
35:11.598 --> 35:14.144
Where else find a senior like me?

828
35:14.144 --> 35:16.768
I used to get beaten here all the time.

829
35:16.768 --> 35:18.738
Want another beating today?

830
35:19.368 --> 35:21.550
Trying to end up in the brig again?

831
35:21.550 --> 35:23.191
Can't have that.

832
35:24.582 --> 35:25.945
Sorry.

833
35:25.945 --> 35:27.545
Man, this is heavy.

834
35:29.603 --> 35:31.687
Come on, let's finish up. Everything going okay up there?

835
35:31.687 --> 35:34.091
- Understood. - Understood.

836
35:34.091 --> 35:35.968
Hey, Bit Na Ri. Try not to kick up so much dust.

837
35:35.968 --> 35:37.747
I'm sorry.

838
35:39.729 --> 35:41.552
When are those guys getting back?

839
35:41.552 --> 35:43.811
They should be here soon.

840
35:43.811 --> 35:45.709
After all this, we should get a nap, right?

841
35:45.709 --> 35:47.020
Nap, my ass.

842
35:47.020 --> 35:49.093
When have we ever gotten one?

843
35:49.093 --> 35:51.526
I'll make sure we get one somehow.

844
35:51.526 --> 35:54.124
Now that's reassuring.

845
35:54.124 --> 35:55.716
Oh, they're back.

846
35:55.716 --> 35:57.579
- Nice work. - Good work, guys.

847
35:57.579 --> 35:58.910
- Thank you. - Private Kim Hyeon Uk.

848
35:58.910 --> 36:00.992
Thank you.

849
36:00.992 --> 36:02.864
You two short-timers.

850
36:02.864 --> 36:05.203
Must've been exhausting resting in the shade.

851
36:05.203 --> 36:07.625
Man, even the shade was hot.

852
36:07.625 --> 36:09.319
We're getting a nap today, right?

853
36:09.319 --> 36:11.085
I really will die if we don't.

854
36:11.085 --> 36:12.995
I almost passed out earlier, I swear.

855
36:12.995 --> 36:14.522
This punk and his whining.

856
36:14.522 --> 36:15.495
I swear it's true.

857
36:15.495 --> 36:17.333
Look at him, still running his mouth.

858
36:17.333 --> 36:18.668
Go ask the admin office later.

859
36:18.668 --> 36:19.618
Yes, sir.

860
36:19.618 --> 36:21.287
All right, good work. Dismissed.

861
36:21.287 --> 36:23.102
- Dismissed. - Thank you, sir.

862
36:23.102 --> 36:24.566
Squad leaders, front of our room.

863
36:24.566 --> 36:26.210
Squad leaders, gather up.

864
36:43.661 --> 36:45.868
30...

865
36:52.711 --> 36:56.637
"Saying we can't nap because of three degrees,

866
36:56.637 --> 36:59.240
that means you squad leaders just aren't good enough,"

867
36:59.240 --> 37:03.848
is what these two short-timers said.

868
37:03.848 --> 37:05.519
- Nice! - You tell them!

869
37:05.519 --> 37:08.684
And "if by some chance we don't get to nap,

870
37:08.684 --> 37:11.547
I'll show you exactly what a short-timer's grief looks like,"

871
37:11.547 --> 37:14.874
they also said, very forcefully.

872
37:14.874 --> 37:16.135
That one's on me.

873
37:16.135 --> 37:19.707
Please, if you don't want to see me act up, I need you all to come through.

874
37:19.707 --> 37:21.722
Show them what squad leaders can do!

875
37:21.722 --> 37:23.547
- Understood. - Understood.

876
37:23.547 --> 37:26.696
Come on, you're supposed to go home quietly. What is this?

877
37:26.696 --> 37:29.211
You have to help me go home quietly.

878
37:29.211 --> 37:31.102
Hey, who's in the admin office today?

879
37:31.102 --> 37:32.081
The platoon leader.

880
37:32.081 --> 37:34.188
Ugh, he's going to do everything by the book.

881
37:34.188 --> 37:36.677
He is. As a matter of fact...

882
37:38.004 --> 37:38.978
Is everyone here?

883
37:38.978 --> 37:40.189
- Yes, sir. - Yes, sir.

884
37:40.189 --> 37:43.247
I will now brief you on the nap policy.

885
37:43.247 --> 37:45.983
Napping in the unit has been raised as an issue several times,

886
37:45.983 --> 37:47.681
due to failure to meet the temperature standard.

887
37:47.681 --> 37:50.375
So, per the corps' proper nap temperature standard,

888
37:50.375 --> 37:52.758
we check the admin office thermometer at exactly 13:00.

889
37:52.758 --> 37:54.614
- 35. - If it's over 35 degrees,

890
37:54.614 --> 37:56.196
we'll take a nap.

891
37:56.196 --> 37:57.703
- Yes, sir. - Yes, sir.

892
37:57.703 --> 38:01.790
But do not ever forget that this nap isn't simply time to sleep in comfort,

893
38:01.790 --> 38:05.758
it's time to recover our combat strength from the extreme heat, got it?

894
38:05.758 --> 38:07.002
- Yes, sir! - Yes, sir!

895
38:07.002 --> 38:10.480
He says no nap unless it's over 35.

896
38:12.918 --> 38:14.805
Huh? 32.

897
38:14.805 --> 38:16.139
32 degrees.

898
38:16.139 --> 38:18.797
Ugh, three degrees.

899
38:18.797 --> 38:20.963
I need to hold a meeting.

900
38:21.967 --> 38:24.470
Before we go to work on the admin office thermometer,

901
38:24.470 --> 38:25.596
let's do our best with that one.

902
38:25.596 --> 38:26.958
Anyone got a good idea?

903
38:26.958 --> 38:29.641
Private Kim Hyeon Uk!

904
38:29.641 --> 38:31.406
Private Kim Hyeon Uk!

905
38:31.406 --> 38:32.877
Go ahead.

906
38:34.316 --> 38:36.259
I'll hold it in my armpit.

907
38:36.871 --> 38:39.938
Come on, you don't have to go that far.

908
38:39.938 --> 38:42.012
This one's easy to raise.

909
38:44.935 --> 38:48.263
Oh, it's going up! It's going up!

910
38:48.263 --> 38:49.895
It's going up?

911
38:52.247 --> 38:54.565
It really is going up.

912
38:54.565 --> 38:56.413
Ah, it's going down.

913
38:56.413 --> 38:58.010
Huh, what?

914
39:00.033 --> 39:03.107
Oh, it's going up. It's going up!

915
39:03.107 --> 39:05.410
It's going up!

916
39:08.079 --> 39:09.641
It's going down.

917
39:09.641 --> 39:11.743
- Ah, come on. - Come on.

918
39:12.502 --> 39:14.561
Stop it, you punk.

919
39:14.561 --> 39:15.875
Oh, it's working.

920
39:15.875 --> 39:17.207
It's going!

921
39:17.207 --> 39:19.946
33, 34!

922
39:21.632 --> 39:23.971
Hey, what's wrong? You okay?

923
39:23.971 --> 39:26.191
It's hyperventilation.

924
39:26.191 --> 39:28.731
- What? - When you blow hard over and over,

925
39:28.731 --> 39:31.087
you hyperventilate, and the carbon dioxide in your blood drops.

926
39:31.087 --> 39:33.851
Then the blood vessels in your brain constrict, and blood flow to the brain drops,

927
39:33.851 --> 39:35.540
which can cause headaches or dizziness.

928
39:35.540 --> 39:36.628
But it's only temporary,

929
39:36.628 --> 39:38.805
so there's no need to worry too much.

930
39:41.338 --> 39:44.068
- Oh. What is he? - I thought the platoon leader possessed him.

931
39:44.068 --> 39:45.843
- You were a science major? - Yes.

932
39:45.843 --> 39:47.677
Right, this punk's good at studying!

933
39:47.677 --> 39:50.589
Hey, let's all try it together. Everyone get on it.

934
39:50.589 --> 39:52.189
Uh, yes.

935
40:02.019 --> 40:03.931
- Garlic breath. - Who is it? It's you, right?

936
40:03.931 --> 40:06.947
- It's not me. - Jeon Sekai, your Buddion breath...

937
40:06.947 --> 40:08.531
Sorry.

938
40:08.531 --> 40:09.710
Let me try again.

939
40:09.710 --> 40:11.291
Again.

940
40:12.111 --> 40:13.787
I don't think this will work.

941
40:13.787 --> 40:16.539
It goes up, but the second we stop blowing, it drops.

942
40:16.539 --> 40:17.582
Wait.

943
40:17.582 --> 40:20.371
What if we just heat it with a lighter?

944
40:20.371 --> 40:21.713
Are you crazy?

945
40:21.713 --> 40:23.788
- Put it out! - I was kidding.

946
40:23.788 --> 40:26.220
How about a hand warmer?

947
40:26.220 --> 40:28.393
- A hand warmer? Nice. - A hand warmer.

948
40:30.898 --> 40:34.079
It's still going up.

949
40:34.079 --> 40:35.673
38, 39...

950
40:35.673 --> 40:37.853
It's 40 degrees.

951
40:37.853 --> 40:39.370
Damn, no.

952
40:39.370 --> 40:41.151
If we're going to fake it, we need to keep it believable.

953
40:41.151 --> 40:43.201
This isn't Africa.

954
40:43.201 --> 40:46.864
How about calling in Min Seok's dad again?

955
40:46.864 --> 40:49.494
If my sister finds out I called him over an afternoon nap,

956
40:49.494 --> 40:52.203
I might end up sleeping forever.

957
40:53.600 --> 40:55.317
Oh, I got it!

958
40:55.317 --> 40:56.719
How about a magnifying glass?

959
40:56.719 --> 40:59.432
- Where are we supposed to get one? - Magnifying glass...

960
41:01.418 --> 41:02.988
These are concave lenses,

961
41:02.988 --> 41:05.522
so I think we'd need reading glasses.

962
41:06.535 --> 41:08.415
But this jerk has no ideas of his own,

963
41:08.415 --> 41:10.677
and all he does is shoot ours down. You want to die?

964
41:10.677 --> 41:11.753
I'm sorry.

965
41:11.753 --> 41:13.558
12:57...

966
41:13.558 --> 41:15.793
Are we really going to lose our nap like this?

967
41:17.404 --> 41:19.519
Then...

968
41:19.519 --> 41:21.271
how about this?

969
41:21.996 --> 41:23.650
Hey, Mom.

970
41:24.607 --> 41:26.418
Did you eat?

971
41:26.418 --> 41:28.803
Of course I ate.

972
41:37.588 --> 41:39.648
I told you to eat on time.

973
41:46.546 --> 41:48.701
Wait...

974
41:57.518 --> 41:59.167
You saw it?

975
42:00.971 --> 42:03.046
No, I mean...

976
42:06.378 --> 42:09.294
I'm not a second lieutenant anymore. I'm a first lieutenant.

977
42:15.105 --> 42:17.938
When have I ever made you worry?

978
42:17.938 --> 42:18.954
13:00!

979
42:18.954 --> 42:22.816
Mom, I'll call you back in a little bit.

980
42:28.639 --> 42:30.136
Please...

981
42:38.164 --> 42:40.946
This is the platoon leader from the admin office.

982
42:45.123 --> 42:48.146
Effective immediately, the afternoon nap period will begin.

983
42:48.146 --> 42:49.350
Repeating.

984
42:49.350 --> 42:53.013
Effective immediately, the afternoon nap period will begin.

985
42:53.910 --> 42:55.005
Hyeon Uk!

986
42:55.005 --> 42:55.951
Sergeant Kim Sang Hun!

987
42:55.951 --> 42:56.905
Hyeon Uk!

988
42:56.905 --> 42:57.903
Sergeant Kim Sang Hun!

989
42:57.903 --> 43:00.311
You're a total ace!

990
43:00.311 --> 43:02.857
Private Kim Hyeon Uk!

991
43:02.857 --> 43:04.186
Thank you!

992
43:04.186 --> 43:05.746
Chungseong! Love you!

993
43:05.746 --> 43:07.415
You should've been in our squad!

994
43:07.415 --> 43:08.778
Thank you!

995
43:08.778 --> 43:10.837
Hot! Get off me!

996
43:10.837 --> 43:11.899
Let's go!

997
43:11.899 --> 43:13.922
- Yeah, let's go! - Take care!

998
43:13.922 --> 43:15.385
Take care!

999
43:15.385 --> 43:17.153
Thank you!

1000
43:41.592 --> 43:44.298
A nap really is the best thing ever.

1001
43:44.298 --> 43:47.084
The platoon leader made first lieutenant and evolved.

1002
43:47.084 --> 43:48.655
But that Sergeant Choi Il Gu,

1003
43:48.655 --> 43:51.981
no, Staff Sergeant Choi Il Gu, we still don't know why he came back?

1004
43:51.981 --> 43:53.688
He won't say even when we ask.

1005
43:53.688 --> 43:56.666
I heard from the guard commander that he got hit with a huge romance scam

1006
43:56.666 --> 43:59.054
and came back because he needed cash right away.

1007
43:59.054 --> 44:00.786
Who falls for that?

1008
44:00.786 --> 44:03.004
Hey, you never know.

1009
44:03.004 --> 44:04.308
Someone lonely, and along comes...

1010
44:04.308 --> 44:06.905
"Oppa, 30 million so I can go to Korea."

1011
44:06.905 --> 44:09.118
"Come on, 30 million just to come to Korea?"

1012
44:09.118 --> 44:12.628
"30 million's cheap. I love you."

1013
44:14.534 --> 44:16.159
"Hey, 30 million, pass!"

1014
44:16.159 --> 44:18.759
That'd knock you halfway out of your mind.

1015
44:18.759 --> 44:21.005
No, from what I heard...

1016
44:21.005 --> 44:23.111
Right, we can trust what our Sekai says.

1017
44:23.111 --> 44:25.096
The day he was discharged...

1018
44:27.286 --> 44:28.842
Hey, Choi Il Gu.

1019
44:28.842 --> 44:31.703
Yes, Sergeant, uh...

1020
44:31.703 --> 44:34.057
civilian Choi Il Gu.

1021
44:34.057 --> 44:35.191
You want to come back?

1022
44:35.191 --> 44:39.035
Come on, what a thing to say on a great day like this.

1023
44:40.345 --> 44:42.196
All right.

1024
44:45.114 --> 44:46.706
Why are you doing this?

1025
44:46.706 --> 44:49.214
You should just re-enlist!

1026
44:49.896 --> 44:51.534
That's not happening.

1027
44:51.534 --> 44:54.734
You going to re-enlist, or hit the car in front?

1028
44:54.734 --> 44:56.722
What are you talking about?

1029
44:56.722 --> 44:58.925
Become a staff sergeant, or drop dead?

1030
44:58.925 --> 45:01.064
I didn't catch that, sir!

1031
45:01.064 --> 45:03.785
Go long-term, or go to your grave?

1032
45:03.785 --> 45:05.266
First Sergeant!

1033
45:05.266 --> 45:06.472
Hurry up and say it!

1034
45:06.472 --> 45:09.457
We're really going to crash!

1035
45:09.457 --> 45:12.289
I'll volunteer!

1036
45:16.672 --> 45:18.594
You chose it.

1037
45:21.178 --> 45:23.219
First Sergeant...

1038
45:23.219 --> 45:25.073
"Become a staff sergeant, or drop dead?"

1039
45:25.073 --> 45:27.048
"Go long-term, or go to your grave,"

1040
45:27.048 --> 45:28.975
is what he said.

1041
45:28.975 --> 45:31.071
"You going to re-enlist, or hit the car in front?"

1042
45:31.071 --> 45:33.772
"Become a staff sergeant, or drop dead?"

1043
45:33.772 --> 45:35.845
This punk's tongue got way longer, seriously.

1044
45:35.845 --> 45:38.215
That punk's tongue really does seem longer now.

1045
45:38.215 --> 45:40.280
He's really weird these days.

1046
45:40.280 --> 45:42.831
That's just what I heard.

1047
45:42.831 --> 45:46.953
Sekai can't pull off the dialect acting.

1048
45:46.953 --> 45:48.416
Just go to sleep.

1049
45:48.416 --> 45:50.288
Yes.

1050
45:51.115 --> 45:52.976
"Become a staff sergeant?"

1051
46:06.165 --> 46:09.271
It's not like I can put gas masks on them.

1052
46:09.271 --> 46:11.294
This is the admin office.

1053
46:11.294 --> 46:13.836
Effective immediately, the afternoon nap is over.

1054
46:13.836 --> 46:16.775
Please assemble for weeding detail.

1055
46:16.775 --> 46:18.813
Repeating.

1056
46:18.813 --> 46:20.320
- Wake up! - Effective immediately,

1057
46:20.320 --> 46:21.761
the afternoon nap is over.

1058
46:21.761 --> 46:24.199
Please assemble for weeding detail.

1059
46:24.199 --> 46:25.801
That is all.

1060
46:28.452 --> 46:30.953
Corporal Park Min Seok.

1061
46:31.665 --> 46:33.208
You need to get up.

1062
46:34.756 --> 46:36.215
What?

1063
46:36.215 --> 46:38.953
Feels like I just closed my eyes.

1064
46:38.953 --> 46:40.941
Sergeant Kim Sang Hun,

1065
46:40.941 --> 46:42.808
I dreamed a ton of tanks were driving by.

1066
46:42.808 --> 46:46.501
"Rumble, rumble, rumble..."

1067
46:46.501 --> 46:49.056
"Clank, clank-clank-clank."

1068
46:49.056 --> 46:50.574
You too?

1069
46:50.574 --> 46:52.258
- Me too. - Really?

1070
46:52.258 --> 46:54.922
- Yeah. - You two were probably driving them.

1071
46:54.922 --> 46:56.805
Sorry, what was that?

1072
46:56.805 --> 46:58.268
Huh? What's wrong?

1073
46:58.268 --> 47:00.146
Never mind. Let's get ready to head out.

1074
47:00.146 --> 47:01.953
- Understood. - Understood.

1075
47:02.612 --> 47:05.591
I'll head out first and get the gear ready with the rookie.

1076
47:05.591 --> 47:07.924
Look at you. You're acting like a senior now.

1077
47:07.924 --> 47:09.464
Thank you.

1078
47:09.464 --> 47:11.186
- Let's go. - Understood.

1079
47:11.186 --> 47:12.412
Hyeon Uk.

1080
47:12.412 --> 47:13.792
Private Kim Hyeon Uk.

1081
47:13.792 --> 47:15.264
Put this on.

1082
47:15.909 --> 47:18.141
- Hyeon Uk. - Private Kim Hyeon Uk.

1083
47:18.141 --> 47:20.998
If you're below corporal, keep your training shirt tucked in.

1084
47:20.998 --> 47:22.598
Understood!

1085
47:27.178 --> 47:28.430
It's because I got fat.

1086
47:28.430 --> 47:30.649
- Sorry. - No.

1087
47:30.649 --> 47:32.641
I was going to go over everything at once,

1088
47:32.641 --> 47:34.596
- but I'll just tell you now. - Understood.

1089
47:34.596 --> 47:36.563
[Rookie Manual, Written by Moon Bit Na Ri, Composed by Moon Bit Na Ri]

1090
47:36.563 --> 47:38.940
♪ You can use the gym and computer room halfway through Private First Class ♪

1091
47:38.940 --> 47:40.525
Understood.

1092
47:40.525 --> 47:42.569
- Chungseong! Love you! - You're here?

1093
47:42.569 --> 47:44.071
[Cyber Knowledge Information Room]

1094
47:44.071 --> 47:46.114
Chungseong! Love you!

1095
47:46.114 --> 47:48.954
♪ No sunscreen until you're a Corporal ♪

1096
47:48.954 --> 47:50.864
Yes, understood.

1097
47:50.864 --> 47:52.203
- ♪ You can use toothpaste and shampoo ♪ - Toothpaste.

1098
47:52.203 --> 47:54.478
- ♪ halfway through Corporal ♪ - Thank you.

1099
47:54.478 --> 47:56.541
Understood.

1100
47:56.541 --> 47:59.294
♪ You can use your left arm while eating as a Sergeant ♪

1101
47:59.294 --> 48:02.571
♪ I'll tell you the rest when you make Private First Class ♪

1102
48:02.571 --> 48:03.882
Yeah!

1103
48:03.882 --> 48:04.732
To be continued...

1104
48:04.732 --> 48:06.149
What are you doing? Hurry up!

1105
48:06.149 --> 48:07.789
Sorry.

1106
48:09.725 --> 48:11.954
Just remember what I told you today.

1107
48:11.954 --> 48:13.583
Understood!

1108
48:17.691 --> 48:18.717
I'm okay.

1109
48:18.717 --> 48:21.765
Technically, you're not allowed to use sunscreen until corporal,

1110
48:21.765 --> 48:23.172
but I'll cover for you.

1111
48:23.172 --> 48:24.198
I'm really okay.

1112
48:24.198 --> 48:26.926
I said it's fine. Put it on.

1113
48:26.926 --> 48:28.526
Thank you.

1114
48:29.687 --> 48:32.568
Man, that feels unfair, huh?

1115
48:32.568 --> 48:34.287
You can put some on too.

1116
48:34.287 --> 48:36.806
Private First Class Moon Bit Na Ri! Thank you!

1117
48:42.048 --> 48:43.994
This is the admin office.

1118
48:43.994 --> 48:46.522
Private Kim Hyeon Uk.

1119
48:46.522 --> 48:48.643
Report to the Company Commander's office immediately.

1120
48:48.643 --> 48:49.903
Repeating.

1121
48:49.903 --> 48:52.757
What did he say?

1122
48:52.757 --> 48:55.308
I think he said Hyeon Uk should report to the Company Commander's office.

1123
48:55.308 --> 48:57.119
- You'd better go. - Understood.

1124
48:57.119 --> 48:59.734
Seriously, I can't understand a word of Yoon Mo's announcements.

1125
48:59.734 --> 49:03.925
Exactly. I just piece together a few words and guess.

1126
49:04.580 --> 49:06.293
Sergeant Kim Sang Hun.

1127
49:09.030 --> 49:10.798
Thank you.

1128
49:14.994 --> 49:16.749
- You put it on. - I got plenty on, thanks to you.

1129
49:16.749 --> 49:19.542
Yeah. You sure did.

1130
49:19.542 --> 49:21.512
You didn't use it all, did you?

1131
49:21.512 --> 49:22.534
Uh, here...

1132
49:22.534 --> 49:24.118
There's some left, right?

1133
49:24.118 --> 49:26.381
There's still some left.

1134
49:26.381 --> 49:27.808
It feels a lot lighter.

1135
49:27.808 --> 49:29.367
I'll work twice as hard.

1136
49:29.367 --> 49:31.498
No, it's fine. You're doing enough already.

1137
49:31.498 --> 49:32.858
Just keep doing what you're doing.

1138
49:32.858 --> 49:34.399
Good job. Get back to what you were doing.

1139
49:34.399 --> 49:36.874
- Understood. - Hurry up. Go.

1140
49:43.987 --> 49:45.364
Want a Choco Pie?

1141
49:45.364 --> 49:46.856
Private Kim Hyeon Uk!

1142
49:46.856 --> 49:48.742
Sorry, what was that?

1143
49:50.037 --> 49:51.133
A Choco Pie.

1144
49:51.133 --> 49:53.391
- Thank you. - Yeah.

1145
49:55.324 --> 49:57.859
I've been saving this one.

1146
49:57.859 --> 49:59.603
- Thank you. - Yeah, go ahead.

1147
49:59.603 --> 50:01.177
Thank you.

1148
50:03.745 --> 50:05.992
Chungseong! Love you! Corporal No Hee Jeong, reporting to the Company Commander's office.

1149
50:05.992 --> 50:07.331
All right. Love you.

1150
50:07.331 --> 50:09.139
Can you help Hyeon Uk with his paperwork?

1151
50:09.139 --> 50:10.909
Understood.

1152
50:14.687 --> 50:16.755
We've got a lot to do.

1153
50:16.755 --> 50:18.349
I'll walk you through it one by one, so follow along.

1154
50:18.349 --> 50:19.297
Understood.

1155
50:19.297 --> 50:20.911
First, see this personal information form?

1156
50:20.911 --> 50:22.981
Fill this out first.

1157
50:22.981 --> 50:26.020
And you also need to complete this health questionnaire.

1158
50:28.601 --> 50:30.513
Yes, that's right.

1159
50:37.369 --> 50:42.478
My biggest goal is to finish my military service without a hitch.

1160
50:49.381 --> 50:50.518
Company Commander, we're all done.

1161
50:50.518 --> 50:52.071
Good work, Hee Jeong.

1162
50:52.071 --> 50:53.362
- Yes. - Good work, Hyeon Uk.

1163
50:53.362 --> 50:55.778
Private Kim Hyeon Uk! Thank you.

1164
50:56.698 --> 50:58.373
- Here you go. - Okay.

1165
51:05.004 --> 51:07.394
Having left basic training once before,

1166
51:07.394 --> 51:10.532
this enlistment means even more to me.

1167
51:13.071 --> 51:15.264
- Keep these safe. - Understood.

1168
51:15.264 --> 51:16.885
All right.

1169
51:16.885 --> 51:20.129
Shall we go perform our sacred new-recruit ritual?

1170
51:22.834 --> 51:25.452
[Sauna]

1171
51:30.703 --> 51:32.208
What are you doing?

1172
51:32.208 --> 51:34.650
- Feeling awkward? - No.

1173
51:34.650 --> 51:37.261
All right. I'll undress first.

1174
51:39.565 --> 51:41.255
There.

1175
51:41.255 --> 51:43.668
See? Take yours off.

1176
51:44.391 --> 51:46.208
Understood.

1177
51:47.983 --> 51:49.939
When a new recruit comes in,

1178
51:49.939 --> 51:51.893
this is a little ritual where you wash off

1179
51:51.893 --> 51:54.277
all the grime from civilian life and are reborn as a soldier.

1180
51:54.277 --> 51:55.571
Don't feel too awkward about it.

1181
51:55.571 --> 51:57.568
- Understood. - Yeah.

1182
51:57.568 --> 51:59.356
Can I ask you one thing?

1183
51:59.356 --> 52:01.220
- What? - Is this a unit tradition?

1184
52:01.220 --> 52:03.204
No. This is the first time.

1185
52:03.204 --> 52:05.832
You're starting the tradition.

1186
52:05.832 --> 52:07.257
So yeah, it's a little awkward,

1187
52:07.257 --> 52:08.560
but still, love you.

1188
52:08.560 --> 52:11.287
Chungseong! Love you!

1189
52:11.287 --> 52:12.726
Yeah. Love you.

1190
52:12.726 --> 52:14.528
Private Kim Hyeon Uk! Thank you.

1191
52:14.528 --> 52:16.941
Man, you're in great shape.

1192
52:16.941 --> 52:18.347
Thank you!

1193
52:18.347 --> 52:21.410
I used to look like that too.

1194
52:21.410 --> 52:22.645
- Let's head in. - Understood.

1195
52:22.645 --> 52:24.040
Yeah.

1196
52:27.185 --> 52:28.387
Been a while since you showered

1197
52:28.387 --> 52:30.953
in nice hot water like this since basic training, right?

1198
52:30.953 --> 52:32.582
Yes.

1199
52:32.582 --> 52:34.694
That explains all this dead skin.

1200
52:34.694 --> 52:36.842
What is this, udon?

1201
52:36.842 --> 52:38.162
I'm sorry.

1202
52:38.162 --> 52:40.867
I haven't had a scrub since I was a kid.

1203
52:40.867 --> 52:43.079
No need to apologize.

1204
52:43.079 --> 52:45.315
- Hyeon Uk. - Private Kim Hyeon Uk.

1205
52:45.315 --> 52:48.651
Whatever you did on the outside, whatever happened in the past,

1206
52:48.651 --> 52:51.682
wash it all away and start fresh here.

1207
52:51.682 --> 52:53.529
Understood!

1208
52:54.754 --> 52:58.468
From now on, we're all in the same boat.

1209
52:58.468 --> 53:00.549
If you have family in civilian life,

1210
53:00.549 --> 53:03.204
your fellow soldiers are your family in the army.

1211
53:03.204 --> 53:07.049
Family bathes together, sleeps together,

1212
53:07.049 --> 53:10.032
cries and laughs together, and gets through things together.

1213
53:10.032 --> 53:12.581
So what do you need to do to get through it together?

1214
53:13.798 --> 53:16.662
I need to work hard and do my best.

1215
53:16.662 --> 53:18.254
That's right.

1216
53:18.254 --> 53:21.330
But don't stress over doing everything perfectly,

1217
53:21.330 --> 53:24.735
and when things get tough, don't try to carry it all by yourself.

1218
53:24.735 --> 53:28.639
That's how you avoid burning out. Got it?

1219
53:29.712 --> 53:32.253
- Understood. - Okay.

1220
53:32.253 --> 53:34.670
All right, switch.

1221
53:34.670 --> 53:36.270
Understood.

1222
53:42.111 --> 53:45.264
- Let's head in. - Oh, nice.

1223
53:45.264 --> 53:46.498
Company Commander?

1224
53:46.498 --> 53:47.906
Oh, fancy seeing you here.

1225
53:47.906 --> 53:50.186
Chungseong! Love you!

1226
53:50.186 --> 53:52.394
- Chungseong! Love you! - Chungseong! Love you!

1227
53:52.394 --> 53:54.469
Yeah, Private Kim Hyeon Uk. We love you too.

1228
53:54.469 --> 53:56.263
- Thank you. - What brings you here?

1229
53:56.263 --> 53:59.287
We played a game of foot volleyball, then came to shower.

1230
53:59.287 --> 54:01.386
After you're done scrubbing the Company Commander's back,

1231
54:01.386 --> 54:02.466
can you scrub mine too?

1232
54:02.466 --> 54:04.206
Understood. I'll scrub you nice and hard.

1233
54:04.206 --> 54:06.887
Okay. I'm already softened up from all the sweat,

1234
54:06.887 --> 54:08.154
- so do me now. - Understood.

1235
54:08.154 --> 54:09.572
Yeah, scrub him first.

1236
54:09.572 --> 54:12.233
I'll just get one turn.

1237
54:14.252 --> 54:16.503
That feels good.

1238
54:17.555 --> 54:19.829
- Hey, Choi Il Gu. - Hey, easy. Yeah.

1239
54:19.829 --> 54:21.561
Don't hog all the pampering. Scrub mine too.

1240
54:21.561 --> 54:23.327
Understood.

1241
54:25.096 --> 54:27.331
Go on. Do it.

1242
54:29.520 --> 54:31.353
That feels good.

1243
54:31.353 --> 54:32.937
- A little harder. - Got it.

1244
54:32.937 --> 54:34.065
Assistant platoon leader,

1245
54:34.065 --> 54:36.114
- how about we scrub each other's backs... - No.

1246
54:36.114 --> 54:37.951
Hey, both of you, come here. I'll scrub you.

1247
54:37.951 --> 54:40.340
- Yes. - Understood.

1248
54:40.340 --> 54:44.266
- Huh? Could you pick up the soap? - Yes, I'll get it.

1249
54:44.266 --> 54:46.631
Hey, you people!

1250
54:46.631 --> 54:49.441
This is getting ridiculous!

1251
54:49.441 --> 54:51.041
Seriously!

1252
54:51.041 --> 54:53.750
What on earth are you doing?

1253
54:53.750 --> 54:55.835
Ugh, I can't stand looking at this.

1254
54:55.835 --> 54:57.666
Why did he get so upset?

1255
54:57.666 --> 54:59.190
Were we too loud?

1256
54:59.190 --> 55:00.886
Well...

1257
55:00.886 --> 55:03.396
Maybe from now on, when we're off base,

1258
55:03.396 --> 55:06.055
we should just say "Chungseong" when we salute.

1259
55:13.876 --> 55:15.829
Buddion's here.

1260
55:16.833 --> 55:19.750
Then I guess I'll take them again.

1261
55:20.619 --> 55:22.631
Thanks, everyone!

1262
55:22.631 --> 55:25.306
No, thank you.

1263
55:27.909 --> 55:29.514
Does that stuff actually taste good?

1264
55:29.514 --> 55:31.471
It's like drinking tear gas.

1265
55:31.471 --> 55:32.600
Gas! Gas! Gas!

1266
55:32.600 --> 55:34.699
I love it.

1267
55:34.699 --> 55:38.804
I wouldn't trade Buddion for any drink in the world.

1268
55:38.804 --> 55:41.120
Even after I get out, I'll drink nothing but Buddion.

1269
55:41.120 --> 55:46.385
Actually, I'd do Buddion ads and take Buddion instead of money.

1270
55:48.343 --> 55:51.416
Real men drink Buddion!

1271
55:58.225 --> 56:02.060
I can't tell if he's adjusted too well or not at all.

1272
56:02.060 --> 56:04.389
I adjusted just fine.

1273
56:04.389 --> 56:05.981
Ugh, that smell.

1274
56:05.981 --> 56:07.121
Sorry.

1275
56:07.121 --> 56:08.547
Man, it's sad.

1276
56:08.547 --> 56:12.118
Once I get out, I'll only see that idiot Se Gye on TV.

1277
56:13.041 --> 56:16.262
Still, I'm glad I can go home knowing Se Gye adjusted well.

1278
56:16.262 --> 56:18.729
What are you going to do when you get out?

1279
56:18.729 --> 56:20.106
Me?

1280
56:23.009 --> 56:24.012
I'm not telling.

1281
56:24.012 --> 56:25.394
Come on. What is it?

1282
56:25.394 --> 56:26.891
Well...

1283
56:27.655 --> 56:29.212
I've been thinking...

1284
56:29.212 --> 56:31.291
Come on, you can tell us.

1285
56:31.291 --> 56:33.373
What is it?

1286
56:33.373 --> 56:35.314
I might take the college entrance exam.

1287
56:35.314 --> 56:37.400
What?

1288
56:37.400 --> 56:38.884
I told you I didn't want to say.

1289
56:38.884 --> 56:40.184
Don't laugh.

1290
56:40.184 --> 56:41.862
I said stop laughing!

1291
56:41.862 --> 56:44.566
It's hot enough without you pissing me off.

1292
56:44.566 --> 56:47.105
Do you want me to help you study?

1293
56:47.105 --> 56:48.721
- Are you any good? - Level eight.

1294
56:48.721 --> 56:50.097
You're still messing with me.

1295
56:50.097 --> 56:51.294
Damn it.

1296
56:51.294 --> 56:53.525
Fine. I'll let it slide.

1297
56:53.525 --> 56:54.560
Love you.

1298
56:54.560 --> 56:56.597
You should know who to trust.

1299
56:58.707 --> 56:59.917
Why is this so good?

1300
56:59.917 --> 57:01.870
Come in. Come on.

1301
57:02.904 --> 57:04.870
- Chungseong! Love you! - Hey, keep it up.

1302
57:04.870 --> 57:06.870
- Thank you. - Hope the workout's going well.

1303
57:06.870 --> 57:08.529
Yeah.

1304
57:08.529 --> 57:09.751
Am I allowed in here?

1305
57:09.751 --> 57:11.117
Of course.

1306
57:11.117 --> 57:13.657
If I say it's okay, it's okay.

1307
57:13.657 --> 57:15.559
Yes.

1308
57:15.559 --> 57:17.764
- Chungseong! Love you! - Oh, Byeong Ho.

1309
57:17.764 --> 57:19.406
Are you finally starting to work out?

1310
57:19.406 --> 57:21.803
- No. - Isn't it about time you did?

1311
57:21.803 --> 57:22.898
You know me.

1312
57:22.898 --> 57:26.543
I gain muscle fast, so I'm taking it slow.

1313
57:27.645 --> 57:29.632
- Hey. - Private Kim Hyeon Uk!

1314
57:29.632 --> 57:31.300
You're only a private, and you're already using the gym?

1315
57:31.300 --> 57:34.324
- I'm sorry! - I brought him, man.

1316
57:34.324 --> 57:36.266
Aren't you giving Hyeon Uk special treatment?

1317
57:36.266 --> 57:37.350
What special treatment?

1318
57:37.350 --> 57:40.320
He's my junior and my boot camp buddy. Of course I look out for him.

1319
57:40.320 --> 57:41.328
Must be nice.

1320
57:41.328 --> 57:44.462
Private Kim Hyeon Uk! Yes, it is!

1321
57:44.462 --> 57:47.548
Anyway, this is the gym.

1322
57:47.548 --> 57:49.091
- Want to see the computer room? - Yes, sounds good.

1323
57:49.091 --> 57:50.481
Let's go check it out.

1324
57:50.481 --> 57:52.111
- Take care. - Take care.

1325
57:52.111 --> 57:53.054
- You too. - Take care.

1326
57:53.054 --> 57:55.239
- Hey, hurry up. - Yes.

1327
58:00.682 --> 58:04.165
Se Gye. Is that T-shirt tan some kind of tattoo?

1328
58:04.165 --> 58:06.763
Forget your boots. You need to scrub that tan off first.

1329
58:06.763 --> 58:10.279
It's a military tattoo money can't buy.

1330
58:10.279 --> 58:12.589
What kind of nonsense is that?

1331
58:14.241 --> 58:18.303
Se Gye practically had a halo when he first arrived.

1332
58:24.293 --> 58:25.628
Now he looks just like us.

1333
58:25.628 --> 58:26.841
Exactly.

1334
58:26.841 --> 58:28.134
Take better care of yourself.

1335
58:28.134 --> 58:30.925
The seniors say they can't tell us apart.

1336
58:30.925 --> 58:32.713
- Come on. - Come on.

1337
58:32.713 --> 58:34.595
That's a stretch. Dial it back.

1338
58:34.595 --> 58:37.491
Come on, don't we look a little alike?

1339
58:38.114 --> 58:40.584
Did you just fart with your mouth?

1340
58:40.584 --> 58:42.369
That punk...

1341
58:44.054 --> 58:45.820
Okay.

1342
58:45.820 --> 58:48.026
- Hey, Se Gye. - Private First Class Jeon Se Gye!

1343
58:48.026 --> 58:49.566
What are you so happy about?

1344
58:49.566 --> 58:52.749
Polishing my combat boots is my favorite part.

1345
58:52.749 --> 58:55.873
I brush off the dirt, polish and buff them

1346
58:55.873 --> 58:58.658
while thinking about what I did wrong,

1347
58:58.658 --> 58:59.971
why I got chewed out again,

1348
58:59.971 --> 59:03.294
and how I could've done better.

1349
59:03.294 --> 59:06.782
It's my time to reflect on myself.

1350
59:06.782 --> 59:08.418
Are you filming a drama?

1351
59:08.418 --> 59:09.813
Is there a camera here or something?

1352
59:09.813 --> 59:12.263
Once I'm done polishing them,

1353
59:12.263 --> 59:15.094
I finally realize what kind of person I am.

1354
59:15.094 --> 59:16.512
Who I am.

1355
59:16.512 --> 59:18.447
Who are you?

1356
59:19.125 --> 59:21.468
Superstar...

1357
59:21.468 --> 59:24.085
Jeon Sekai.

1358
59:24.085 --> 59:26.049
I think this guy's completely lost it.

1359
59:26.049 --> 59:27.446
He needs to see a doctor.

1360
59:27.446 --> 59:28.791
Come on, seriously.

1361
59:28.791 --> 59:30.968
I'm fine.

1362
59:32.820 --> 59:35.121
You've got Min Seok, plus Da Hye a year ahead of you.

1363
59:35.121 --> 59:36.536
Hyeon Uk, you've got it made in the army.

1364
59:36.536 --> 59:39.007
They're both really good to me.

1365
59:39.007 --> 59:41.941
I'll have a one-year junior coming in soon too.

1366
59:41.941 --> 59:45.166
I'm going to treat him well.

1367
59:45.166 --> 59:46.795
Chungseong! Love you!

1368
59:46.795 --> 59:49.190
Are you on the first watch?

1369
59:49.190 --> 59:51.070
That's right.

1370
59:51.070 --> 59:52.657
What's this?

1371
59:52.657 --> 59:54.901
Please go easy on Hyeon Uk.

1372
59:54.901 --> 59:57.042
He's not you. What would I give him crap for?

1373
59:57.042 --> 59:58.106
He's A-tier.

1374
59:58.106 --> 59:59.860
Corporal Ji Jeong Min, aren't you B-tier?

1375
59:59.860 --> 01:00:00.902
What?

1376
01:00:00.902 --> 01:00:03.334
I'm C-tier, idiot.

1377
01:00:04.445 --> 01:00:07.965
No matter how hard you two try, you won't be half as good as Se Gye.

1378
01:00:07.965 --> 01:00:09.494
Se Gye, who are you?

1379
01:00:09.494 --> 01:00:12.739
Special Warrior Jeon Sekai.

1380
01:00:13.671 --> 01:00:15.988
Oppa, I love you!

1381
01:00:15.988 --> 01:00:17.611
Please be quiet.

1382
01:00:18.281 --> 01:00:20.743
Se Gye's a total surprise, right?

1383
01:00:20.743 --> 01:00:22.010
Yes.

1384
01:00:22.010 --> 01:00:23.458
He's a full-on soldier now.

1385
01:00:23.458 --> 01:00:25.231
I'm not even surprised anymore.

1386
01:00:25.231 --> 01:00:27.124
I still am.

1387
01:00:27.124 --> 01:00:28.330
Oh, right.

1388
01:00:28.330 --> 01:00:29.616
Did you make your call today?

1389
01:00:29.616 --> 01:00:31.191
Not yet.

1390
01:00:31.191 --> 01:00:34.588
What? You should've told me.

1391
01:00:34.588 --> 01:00:37.125
Roll call's in ten minutes. Let's go make your call.

1392
01:00:37.125 --> 01:00:39.502
I'm okay. Really.

1393
01:00:39.502 --> 01:00:41.838
No, I'll cover for you. Come on. Let's go.

1394
01:00:41.838 --> 01:00:43.630
Great, no one's here.

1395
01:00:43.630 --> 01:00:45.382
- Go in here and make your call. - Yes.

1396
01:00:45.382 --> 01:00:47.444
- Use mine. - It's okay.

1397
01:00:47.444 --> 01:00:49.159
No, use it. Hurry. We're out of time.

1398
01:00:49.159 --> 01:00:50.662
Yes.

1399
01:00:56.695 --> 01:00:58.695
Good.

1400
01:00:58.695 --> 01:01:00.640
- Chungseong! Love you! - Chungseong! Love you!

1401
01:01:00.640 --> 01:01:02.696
- Hope your shift's going well. - Here to make a call?

1402
01:01:02.696 --> 01:01:03.920
- Yes. - Go ahead.

1403
01:01:03.920 --> 01:01:05.862
- Go make your call. - Yes.

1404
01:01:06.542 --> 01:01:08.276
Aren't you calling?

1405
01:01:08.276 --> 01:01:11.235
No, I'm just here so Hyeon Uk can call.

1406
01:01:13.469 --> 01:01:15.795
Aren't you being a little too nice to Hyeon Uk?

1407
01:01:15.795 --> 01:01:19.627
Hey, want to hear something really funny?

1408
01:01:19.627 --> 01:01:22.329
- Here... - What the...

1409
01:01:41.272 --> 01:01:43.336
Hey, sis.

1410
01:01:43.336 --> 01:01:45.227
When did you say you were coming?

1411
01:01:46.783 --> 01:01:49.300
Oh, right.

1412
01:01:49.300 --> 01:01:50.900
How's Mom?

1413
01:02:03.911 --> 01:02:05.717
Chungseong! What brings you here?

1414
01:02:05.717 --> 01:02:08.952
I'm the battalion commander taking over tomorrow.

1415
01:02:11.339 --> 01:02:13.172
Chungseong!

1416
01:02:14.125 --> 01:02:17.062
All right. Carry on.

1417
01:02:17.062 --> 01:02:18.781
Excuse me,

1418
01:02:18.781 --> 01:02:20.717
but even as battalion commander,

1419
01:02:20.717 --> 01:02:23.390
may I have your rank and name?

1420
01:02:31.065 --> 01:02:32.376
Lieutenant Colonel Byeon Hyeok Jin.

1421
01:02:32.376 --> 01:02:34.935
Chungseong! Thank you!

1422
01:02:36.982 --> 01:02:38.559
What's your name?

1423
01:02:38.559 --> 01:02:40.868
Staff Sergeant Kim Tae Hoon!

1424
01:02:40.868 --> 01:02:44.223
- Kim Tae Hoon, Staff Sergeant. - Staff Sergeant Kim Tae Hoon!

1425
01:02:44.223 --> 01:02:46.547
Thanks for staying sharp on duty.

1426
01:02:46.547 --> 01:02:48.274
Keep it up.

1427
01:02:48.274 --> 01:02:50.592
Staff Sergeant Kim Tae Hoon!

1428
01:02:50.592 --> 01:02:51.786
I'll do my best!

1429
01:02:51.786 --> 01:02:52.964
All right.

1430
01:02:52.964 --> 01:02:57.068
The light at the guard post is flickering.

1431
01:02:57.068 --> 01:02:59.348
Make sure you pass that on at tomorrow's shift change.

1432
01:02:59.348 --> 01:03:00.364
Yes.

1433
01:03:00.364 --> 01:03:02.372
All right. Carry on.

1434
01:03:07.252 --> 01:03:09.186
Chungseong!

1435
01:03:17.538 --> 01:03:19.745
- Who was that? - What?

1436
01:03:19.745 --> 01:03:22.627
The new battalion commander. He takes over tomorrow.

1437
01:03:22.627 --> 01:03:24.410
Why'd he come this late?

1438
01:03:24.410 --> 01:03:25.785
No idea.

1439
01:03:25.785 --> 01:03:29.398
But that suit, that car...

1440
01:03:29.398 --> 01:03:31.425
He's got serious presence.

1441
01:03:34.208 --> 01:03:36.404
When did he even notice that?

1442
01:03:36.404 --> 01:03:38.834
Oh, right. I should call ahead.

1443
01:03:38.834 --> 01:03:42.791
[Devotion to the Nation]

1444
01:04:23.810 --> 01:04:25.470
Who are you?

1445
01:04:31.327 --> 01:04:33.145
Me?

1446
01:04:33.145 --> 01:04:35.214
The new battalion commander.

1447
01:04:35.214 --> 01:04:36.820
They say he's a total hotshot.

1448
01:04:36.820 --> 01:04:38.231
I heard it from Yoon Mo too.

1449
01:04:38.231 --> 01:04:40.502
Apparently, he's seriously intimidating.

1450
01:04:42.459 --> 01:04:44.798
Chungseong! Love you!

1451
01:04:44.798 --> 01:04:47.858
Corporal Park Min Seok! No incidents to report!

1452
01:04:50.534 --> 01:04:51.543
Park Min Seok?

1453
01:04:51.543 --> 01:04:54.374
Corporal Park Min Seok!
